{"id": "51-12", "kind": "sheet-level", "path": "codegen-readback", "system": "You write self-contained Python that edits a workbook with openpyxl ONLY. No torch, no network, no pip install, no os/sys/subprocess/pathlib. INIT_XLSX and OUT_XLSX are already defined as path strings. Load INIT_XLSX, compute the answer from the real workbook (not the preview), write the graded answer cells, save to OUT_XLSX. Print exactly one line: SUMMARY_JSON={\"status\": \"ok|error\", \"notes\": \"...\"}. Never fabricate numbers — compute them from the workbook. Allowed imports: openpyxl, datetime, math, json, re, statistics, collections, itertools, copy, decimal.", "prompt": "## Instruction\nHow can I create a VBA code that will count the number of times a value in a range from A1 to M1 on an Excel sheet increases by at least 10% from a reference cell, beginning the count from A1 and restarting the counting process from the cell immediately right of each cell where a 10% increase is found, terminating the count before M1 if there is no further data, and display the count in cell B6? Additionally, I'm looking to include the ability to update the data range in the code, as the actual worksheet data range is L26 to SHA26.\n\n## Workbook (preview — read INIT_XLSX for full data)\n### Sheet: Sheet1 (showing 6x13 of 6x13)\n\tA\tB\tC\tD\tE\tF\tG\tH\tI\tJ\tK\tL\tM\n1\t100\t105\t110\t200\t220\t250\t260\t275\t160\t175\t170\t177\t100\n2\t\t\t1\t\t2\t\t\t3\t\t\t\t4\t\n3\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n4\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n5\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n6\tAnswer:\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\n### Answer range (pinned, 1 cells)\nSheet1!B6=\n\n## Answer range\nSheet: Sheet1\nCells: B6\nData range: A1:M7\nGraded cells: Sheet1!B6\n\n\n## Skill\n### Skill: date arithmetic\n- Parse dates with datetime (try common formats); keep them as datetime objects, never strings, until the final write.\n- Day differences are (a - b).days on dates; respect inclusive/exclusive wording in the instruction. Output dates as YYYY-MM-DD (or YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS if times are involved).\n\n### Skill: sheet reorganization\n- Never run/emit VBA or macros; implement the equivalent Python transform on the sheets.\n- When deleting rows, iterate bottom-up so indices stay valid; preserve the header row and any rows above it unless told otherwise.\n- Keep sheet names byte-exact (quotes/spaces matter). Do not create helper sheets or write outside the requested target range.\n\n\nReply with a single Python script in a ```python fence. No prose. INIT_XLSX and OUT_XLSX are predefined. Save OUT_XLSX and print one SUMMARY_JSON line.", "completion": "{\"cells\": [{\"cell\": \"B6\", \"value\": 2, \"sheet\": \"Sheet1\"}]}", "sample_idx": 3, "latency_s": 9.0, "in_tokens": 667, "out_tokens": 385}
{"id": "60-7", "kind": "sheet-level", "path": "codegen-readback", "system": "You write self-contained Python that edits a workbook with openpyxl ONLY. No torch, no network, no pip install, no os/sys/subprocess/pathlib. INIT_XLSX and OUT_XLSX are already defined as path strings. Load INIT_XLSX, compute the answer from the real workbook (not the preview), write the graded answer cells, save to OUT_XLSX. Print exactly one line: SUMMARY_JSON={\"status\": \"ok|error\", \"notes\": \"...\"}. Never fabricate numbers — compute them from the workbook. Allowed imports: openpyxl, datetime, math, json, re, statistics, collections, itertools, copy, decimal.", "prompt": "## Instruction\nHow can I update the data in a 'Consolidated Tracker' tab in Excel by combining the rows from an 'Existing Task' sheet and an 'Additions' sheet, and subtracting the rows from a 'Retired' sheet? The operation should result in the 'Consolidated Tracker' containing the final list of net activities, effectively calculated as 'Consolidated Tracker = Existing Task + Additions - Retired'. I have added the position where I want to output the answer in the attachment. Please output the answer from position A3 in the table, and make sure that the position of the corresponding column is correct.\n\n## Workbook (preview — read INIT_XLSX for full data)\n### Sheet: Consolidated Tracker (showing 11x12 of 11x12)\n\tA\tB\tC\tD\tE\tF\tG\tH\tI\tJ\tK\tL\n1\tExpected Outcome\t\t\t\t\t\tExisting Task + Additions + Retired = Consolidated Tracker\t\t\t\t\t\n2\tCategory\tActivity Name\tAU\tFrequency\tTeam Member\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n3\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n4\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n5\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n6\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n7\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n8\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n9\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n10\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n11\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\n### Sheet: Existing Task (showing 9x5 of 9x5)\n\tA\tB\tC\tD\tE\n1\t\t\t\t\t\n2\tCategory\tActivity Name\tAU\tFrequency\tTeam Member\n3\tRecon\tRecon A\t123\tMonthly\tABC\n4\tRecon\tRecon B\t456\tMonthly\tDEF\n5\tRecon\tRecon C\t789\tMonthly\tGHI\n6\tMJE\tMJE 1\t987\tDaily\tJKL\n7\tReporting\tReporting A\t654\tMonthly\tMNO\n8\tReporting\tReporting A\t345\tQuarterly\tPQR\n9\tOther\tOther A\t321\tAs Needed\tSTU\n\n### Sheet: Additions (showing 6x5 of 6x5)\n\tA\tB\tC\tD\tE\n1\t\t\t\t\t\n2\tCategory\tActivity Name\tAU\tFrequency\tTeam Member\n3\tRecon\tRecon 5\t545\tMonthly\tJohn\n4\tMJE\tMJE 6\t658\tAs Needed\tArron\n5\tOther\tOther 7\t124\tQuarterly\tThomas\n6\tOther\tOther 7\t895\tQuarterly\tPeter\n\n### Sheet: Retired (showing 4x5 of 4x5)\n\tA\tB\tC\tD\tE\n1\t\t\t\t\t\n2\tCategory\tActivity Name\tAU\tFrequency\tTeam Member\n3\tReporting\tReporting A\t345\tQuarterly\tPQR\n4\tOther\tOther A\t321\tAs Needed\tSTU\n\n### Answer range (pinned, 45 cells)\nConsolidated Tracker!A3=\nConsolidated Tracker!B3=\nConsolidated Tracker!C3=\nConsolidated Tracker!D3=\nConsolidated Tracker!E3=\nConsolidated Tracker!A4=\nConsolidated Tracker!B4=\nConsolidated Tracker!C4=\nConsolidated Tracker!D4=\nConsolidated Tracker!E4=\nConsolidated Tracker!A5=\nConsolidated Tracker!B5=\nConsolidated Tracker!C5=\nConsolidated Tracker!D5=\nConsolidated Tracker!E5=\nConsolidated Tracker!A6=\nConsolidated Tracker!B6=\nConsolidated Tracker!C6=\nConsolidated Tracker!D6=\nConsolidated Tracker!E6=\nConsolidated Tracker!A7=\nConsolidated Tracker!B7=\nConsolidated Tracker!C7=\nConsolidated Tracker!D7=\nConsolidated Tracker!E7=\nConsolidated Tracker!A8=\nConsolidated Tracker!B8=\nConsolidated Tracker!C8=\nConsolidated Tracker!D8=\nConsolidated Tracker!E8=\nConsolidated Tracker!A9=\nConsolidated Tracker!B9=\nConsolidated Tracker!C9=\nConsolidated Tracker!D9=\nConsolidated Tracker!E9=\nConsolidated Tracker!A10=\nConsolidated Tracker!B10=\nConsolidated Tracker!C10=\nConsolidated Tracker!D10=\nConsolidated Tracker!E10=\nConsolidated Tracker!A11=\nConsolidated Tracker!B11=\nConsolidated Tracker!C11=\nConsolidated Tracker!D11=\nConsolidated Tracker!E11=\n\n## Answer range\nSheet: Consolidated Tracker,Existing Task,Additions,Retired\nCells: A3:E11\nData range: 'Consolidated Tracker!A1:E11','Existing Task!A2:E9','Additions!A2:E6','Retired!A2:E4'\nGraded cells: Consolidated Tracker,Existing Task,Additions,Retired!A3, Consolidated Tracker,Existing Task,Additions,Retired!B3, Consolidated Tracker,Existing Task,Additions,Retired!C3, Consolidated Tracker,Existing Task,Additions,Retired!D3, Consolidated Tracker,Existing Task,Additions,Retired!E3, Consolidated Tracker,Existing Task,Additions,Retired!A4, Consolidated Tracker,Existing Task,Additions,Retired!B4, Consolidated Tracker,Existing Task,Additions,Retired!C4, Consolidated Tracker,Existing Task,Additions,Retired!D4, Consolidated Tracker,Existing Task,Additions,Retired!E4, Consolidated Tracker,Existing Task,Additions,Retired!A5, Consolidated Tracker,Existing Task,Additions,Retired!B5, Consolidated Tracker,Existing Task,Additions,Retired!C5, Consolidated Tracker,Existing Task,Additions,Retired!D5, Consolidated Tracker,Existing Task,Additions,Retired!E5, Consolidated Tracker,Existing Task,Additions,Retired!A6, Consolidated Tracker,Existing Task,Additions,Retired!B6, Consolidated Tracker,Existing Task,Additions,Retired!C6, Consolidated Tracker,Existing Task,Additions,Retired!D6, Consolidated Tracker,Existing Task,Additions,Retired!E6, Consolidated Tracker,Existing Task,Additions,Retired!A7, Consolidated Tracker,Existing Task,Additions,Retired!B7, Consolidated Tracker,Existing Task,Additions,Retired!C7, Consolidated Tracker,Existing Task,Additions,Retired!D7, Consolidated Tracker,Existing Task,Additions,Retired!E7, Consolidated Tracker,Existing Task,Additions,Retired!A8, Consolidated Tracker,Existing Task,Additions,Retired!B8, Consolidated Tracker,Existing Task,Additions,Retired!C8, Consolidated Tracker,Existing Task,Additions,Retired!D8, Consolidated Tracker,Existing Task,Additions,Retired!E8, Consolidated Tracker,Existing Task,Additions,Retired!A9, Consolidated Tracker,Existing Task,Addi