{"id": "267-18", "kind": "sheet-level", "path": "codegen-readback", "system": "You write self-contained Python that edits a workbook with openpyxl ONLY. No torch, no network, no pip install, no os/sys/subprocess/pathlib. INIT_XLSX and OUT_XLSX are already defined as path strings. Load INIT_XLSX, compute the answer from the real workbook (not the preview), write the graded answer cells, save to OUT_XLSX. Print exactly one line: SUMMARY_JSON={\"status\": \"ok|error\", \"notes\": \"...\"}. Never fabricate numbers — compute them from the workbook. Allowed imports: openpyxl, datetime, math, json, re, statistics, collections, itertools, copy, decimal.", "prompt": "## Instruction\nI have an Excel sheet where I am concatenating strings in column G in the format [\"/out/\",\"https://theurl.top/images/2.jpg \", \"text?\", \"text!\"]. I need to add a prefix \"//\" to this concatenation pattern (eg, //[ ), Apply formula but only for rows that are highlighted with a yellow color. How can I accomplish this? Could you implement this based on my description?\n\n## Workbook (preview — read INIT_XLSX for full data)\n### Sheet: Folha1 (showing 2x10 of 2x10)\n\tA\tB\tC\tD\tE\tF\tG\tH\tI\tJ\n1\tpath2img&track\t \talt-text\t \t/link/\t \t[\"/link/\", \"path2img&track/path2img&track\", \"alt-text\", \"path2img&track\"],\t\t\t \n2\tpath2img&track2\t \talt-text?\t \t/link/\t \t[\"/link/\", \"path2img&track/path2img&track2\", \"alt-text?\", \"path2img&track2\"],\t\t\t \n\n### Sheet: Folha1 highlighted cells: G1=FF00B050, A2=FFFFFF00, B2=FFFFFF00, C2=FFFFFF00, D2=FFFFFF00, E2=FFFFFF00, F2=FFFFFF00, G2=FFFFFF00, H2=FFFFFF00, I2=FFFFFF00, J2=FFFFFF00\n\n### Answer range (pinned, 2 cells)\nFolha1!G1=[\"/link/\", \"path2img&track/path2img&track\", \"alt-text\", \"path2img&track\"],\nFolha1!G2=[\"/link/\", \"path2img&track/path2img&track2\", \"alt-text?\", \"path2img&track2\"],\n\n## Answer range\nSheet: Folha1\nCells: G1:G2\nData range: A1:G2\nGraded cells: Folha1!G1, Folha1!G2\n\n\n## Skill\n### Skill: formatting-gated logic\n- The instruction gates on cell appearance (highlight/fill/color). Read each cell's fill color (openpyxl `cell.fill.start_color.rgb`) and apply the transform ONLY to cells whose fill matches the stated color.\n\n### Skill: writing cells\n- Write computed VALUES (not formulas) unless the task explicitly requires formula text.\n- Write every requested answer cell; an unwritten cell scores zero. Convert Python types to plain scalars (no numpy types, no datetime objects — use ISO strings).\n\n\nReply with a single Python script in a ```python fence. No prose. INIT_XLSX and OUT_XLSX are predefined. Save OUT_XLSX and print one SUMMARY_JSON line.", "completion": "{\"cells\": [{\"cell\": \"G1\", \"value\": \"=CONCATENATE(\\\"[\\\",\\\"\\\"\\\"\\\",E1,\\\"\\\"\\\"\\\",\\\", \\\"\\\"\\\"&I$1&\\\"\\\",A$1,\\\"/\\\",A1,\\\"\\\"\\\", \\\"\\\"\\\"&C1&\\\"\\\"\\\", \\\"\\\"\\\"&A1&\\\"\\\"\\\"],\\\")\", \"sheet\": \"Folha1\"}, {\"cell\": \"G2\", \"value\": \"=CONCATENATE(\\\"[\\\",\\\"\\\"\\\"\\\",E2,\\\"\\\"\\\"\\\",\\\", \\\"\\\"\\\"&I$1&\\\"\\\",A$1,\\\"/\\\",A2,\\\"\\\"\\\", \\\"\\\"\\\"&C2&\\\"\\\"\\\", \\\"\\\"\\\"&A2&\\\"\\\"\\\"],\\\")\", \"sheet\": \"Folha1\"}]}", "sample_idx": 0, "latency_s": 8.3, "in_tokens": 752, "out_tokens": 257}
{"id": "267-21", "kind": "sheet-level", "path": "codegen-readback", "system": "You write self-contained Python that edits a workbook with openpyxl ONLY. No torch, no network, no pip install, no os/sys/subprocess/pathlib. INIT_XLSX and OUT_XLSX are already defined as path strings. Load INIT_XLSX, compute the answer from the real workbook (not the preview), write the graded answer cells, save to OUT_XLSX. Print exactly one line: SUMMARY_JSON={\"status\": \"ok|error\", \"notes\": \"...\"}. Never fabricate numbers — compute them from the workbook. Allowed imports: openpyxl, datetime, math, json, re, statistics, collections, itertools, copy, decimal.", "prompt": "## Instruction\nHow can I create a comprehensive report in a single sheet ('sheet merging') in Excel that compiles data from multiple sheets, with each sheet representing monthly data that will be added every month, and ensure that the merged report sheet updates as new data is added in the subsequent monthly sheets?  Please output the answer in the corresponding positions of columns C and D in the table, and pay attention to the mapping between the answer and column name and row value. Basically, look up ID from Column B and place the corresponding QTY value from SH1 into Column C and from RP1 into Column D. If there's an error or blank, insert \"-\".\n\n## Workbook (preview — read INIT_XLSX for full data)\n### Sheet: SH1 (showing 8x3 of 8x3)\n\tA\tB\tC\n1\tITEM\tID\tQTY\n2\t1\tMT ASGL-VEN SD-1\t12\n3\t2\tC-ZER\t130\n4\t3\tBB 2000MN TT GH\t90\n5\t4\tBD 234 NH GG\t78\n6\t5\tDEWR 1222** SS TF HJK\t34\n7\t6\tBR 111/33M ER HJ\t66\n8\t7\tVB 1222** SS TF HJK\t45\n\n### Sheet: RP1 (showing 9x3 of 9x3)\n\tA\tB\tC\n1\tITEM\tID\tQTY\n2\t1\tMT ASGL-VEN SD-1\t10\n3\t2\tC-ZER\t15\n4\t3\tBR 111/33M ER HJ\t80\n5\t4\tVB 145** SS TF HJK\t45\n6\t5\tDEWR 1222** SS TF HJK\t34\n7\t6\tDAS 1222** SS TF HJK\t35\n8\t7\tTRM 2000MN TT GH\t16\n9\t8\tBD 234 NH GG\t70\n\n### Sheet: merging (showing 11x4 of 11x4)\n\tA\tB\tC\tD\n1\tITEM\tID\tMONTH1\tMONTH2\n2\t1\tMT ASGL-VEN SD-1\t\t\n3\t2\tC-ZER\t\t\n4\t3\tBB 2000MN TT GH\t\t\n5\t4\tBD 234 NH GG\t\t\n6\t5\tDEWR 1222** SS TF HJK\t\t\n7\t6\tBR 111/33M ER HJ\t\t\n8\t7\tVB 1222** SS TF HJK\t\t\n9\t8\tVB 145** SS TF HJK\t\t\n10\t9\tDAS 1222** SS TF HJK\t\t\n11\t10\tTRM 2000MN TT GH\t\t\n\n### Answer range (pinned, 20 cells)\nmerging!C2=\nmerging!D2=\nmerging!C3=\nmerging!D3=\nmerging!C4=\nmerging!D4=\nmerging!C5=\nmerging!D5=\nmerging!C6=\nmerging!D6=\nmerging!C7=\nmerging!D7=\nmerging!C8=\nmerging!D8=\nmerging!C9=\nmerging!D9=\nmerging!C10=\nmerging!D10=\nmerging!C11=\nmerging!D11=\n\n## Answer range\nSheet: 'SH1','RP1','merging'\nCells: merging'!C2:D11\nData range: SH1!A1:C8','RP1!A1:C8','merging!A1:D11'\nGraded cells: merging!C2, merging!D2, merging!C3, merging!D3, merging!C4, merging!D4, merging!C5, merging!D5, merging!C6, merging!D6, merging!C7, merging!D7, merging!C8, merging!D8, merging!C9, merging!D9, merging!C10, merging!D10, merging!C11, merging!D11\n\n\n## Skill\n### Skill: date arithmetic\n- Parse dates with datetime (try common formats); keep them as datetime objects, never strings, until the final write.\n- Day differences are (a - b).days on dates; respect inclusive/exclusive wording in the instruction. Output dates as YYYY-MM-DD (or YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS if times are involved).\n\n### Skill: sheet reorganization\n- Never run/emit VBA or macros; implement the equivalent Python transform on the sheets.\n- When deleting rows, iterate bottom-up so indices stay valid; preserve the header row and any rows above it unless told otherwise.\n- Keep sheet names byte-exact (quotes/spaces matter). Do not create helper sheets or write outside the requested target range.\n\n\nReply with a single Python script in a ```python fence. No prose. INIT_XLSX and OUT_XLSX are predefined. Save OUT_XLSX and print one SUMMARY_JSON line.", "completion": "{\"cells\": [{\"cell\": \"C2\", \"value\": 12, \"sheet\": \"merging\"}, {\"cell\": \"D2\", \"value\": 10, \"sheet\": \"merging\"}, {\"cell\": \"C3\", \"value\": 130, \"sheet\": \"merging\"}, {\"cell\": \"D3\", \"value\": 15, \"sheet\": \"merging\"}, {\"cell\": \"C4\", \"value\": 90, \"sheet\": \"merging\"}, {\"cell\": \"D4\", \"value\": \"-\", \"sheet\": \"merging\"}, {\"cell\": \"C5\", \"value\": 78, \"sheet\": \"merging\"}, {\"cell\": \"D5\", \"value\": 70, \"sheet\": \"merging\"}, {\"cell\": \"C6\", \"value\": 34, \"sheet\": \"merging\"}, {\"cell\": \"D6\", \"value\": 34, \"sheet\": \"merging\"}, {\"cell\": \"C7\", \"value\": 66, \"sheet\": \"merging\"}, {\"cell\": \"D7\", \"value\": 80, \"sheet\": \"merging\"}, {\"cell\": \"C8\", \"value\": 45, \"sheet\": \"merging\"}, {\"cell\": \"D8\", \"value\": \"-\", \"sheet\": \"merging\"}, {\"cell\": \"C9\", \"value\": \"-\", \"sheet\": \"merging\"}, {\"cell\": \"D9\", \"value\": 45, \"sheet\": \"merging\"}, {\"cell\": \"C10\", \"value\": \"-\", \"sheet\": \"merging\"}, {\"cell\": \"D10\", \"value\": 35, \"sheet\": \"merging\"}, {\"cell\": \"C11\", \"value\": \"-\", \"sheet\": \"merging\"}, {\"cell\": \"D11\", \"value\": 16, \"sheet\": \"merging\"}]}", "sample_idx": 4, "latency_s": 9.4, "in_tokens": 1319, "out_tokens": 368}
