{"id": "269-44", "kind": "sheet-level", "path": "codegen-readback", "system": "You write self-contained Python that edits a workbook with openpyxl ONLY. No torch, no network, no pip install, no os/sys/subprocess/pathlib. INIT_XLSX and OUT_XLSX are already defined as path strings. Load INIT_XLSX, compute the answer from the real workbook (not the preview), write the graded answer cells, save to OUT_XLSX. Print exactly one line: SUMMARY_JSON={\"status\": \"ok|error\", \"notes\": \"...\"}. Never fabricate numbers — compute them from the workbook. Allowed imports: openpyxl, datetime, math, json, re, statistics, collections, itertools, copy, decimal.", "prompt": "## Instruction\nIn my Excel sheet named 'Import Data,' I am trying to create a macro that will delete the four rows located immediately before each instance of the text 'Chassis' in column A. Make sure that the two \"Chassis\" texts are located in A2 & A3.  However, my current VBA code is not functioning properly. Can someone assist me in correcting this code so that it will carry out the task as intended?\n\n## Workbook (preview — read INIT_XLSX for full data)\n### Sheet: Sheet1 (showing 15x1 of 15x1)\n\tA\n1\t\n2\t2022/04/22\n3\t1 - PTR\n4\tX1-BR1\n5\t\n6\tChassis\n7\t\n8\t\n9\t\n10\t\n11\t2022/04/22\n12\t1 - BWE\n13\tX2 -BR2\n14\t\n15\tChassis\n\n### Answer range (pinned, 15 cells)\nSheet1!A1=\nSheet1!A2=2022/04/22\nSheet1!A3=1 - PTR\nSheet1!A4=X1-BR1\nSheet1!A5=\nSheet1!A6=Chassis\nSheet1!A7=\nSheet1!A8=\nSheet1!A9=\nSheet1!A10=\nSheet1!A11=2022/04/22\nSheet1!A12=1 - BWE\nSheet1!A13=X2 -BR2\nSheet1!A14=\nSheet1!A15=Chassis\n\n## Answer range\nSheet: Sheet1\nCells: A1:A15\nData range: A1:A15\nGraded cells: Sheet1!A1, Sheet1!A2, Sheet1!A3, Sheet1!A4, Sheet1!A5, Sheet1!A6, Sheet1!A7, Sheet1!A8, Sheet1!A9, Sheet1!A10, Sheet1!A11, Sheet1!A12, Sheet1!A13, Sheet1!A14, Sheet1!A15\n\n\n## Skill\n### Skill: sheet reorganization\n- Never run/emit VBA or macros; implement the equivalent Python transform on the sheets.\n- When deleting rows, iterate bottom-up so indices stay valid; preserve the header row and any rows above it unless told otherwise.\n- Keep sheet names byte-exact (quotes/spaces matter). Do not create helper sheets or write outside the requested target range.\n\n### Skill: writing cells\n- Write computed VALUES (not formulas) unless the task explicitly requires formula text.\n- Write every requested answer cell; an unwritten cell scores zero. Convert Python types to plain scalars (no numpy types, no datetime objects — use ISO strings).\n\n\nReply with a single Python script in a ```python fence. No prose. INIT_XLSX and OUT_XLSX are predefined. Save OUT_XLSX and print one SUMMARY_JSON line.", "completion": "{\"cells\": [{\"cell\": \"A1\", \"value\": null, \"sheet\": \"Sheet1\"}, {\"cell\": \"A2\", \"value\": \"Chassis\", \"sheet\": \"Sheet1\"}, {\"cell\": \"A3\", \"value\": null, \"sheet\": \"Sheet1\"}, {\"cell\": \"A4\", \"value\": null, \"sheet\": \"Sheet1\"}, {\"cell\": \"A5\", \"value\": null, \"sheet\": \"Sheet1\"}, {\"cell\": \"A6\", \"value\": null, \"sheet\": \"Sheet1\"}, {\"cell\": \"A7\", \"value\": \"Chassis\", \"sheet\": \"Sheet1\"}, {\"cell\": \"A8\", \"value\": null, \"sheet\": \"Sheet1\"}, {\"cell\": \"A9\", \"value\": null, \"sheet\": \"Sheet1\"}, {\"cell\": \"A10\", \"value\": null, \"sheet\": \"Sheet1\"}, {\"cell\": \"A11\", \"value\": null, \"sheet\": \"Sheet1\"}, {\"cell\": \"A12\", \"value\": null, \"sheet\": \"Sheet1\"}, {\"cell\": \"A13\", \"value\": null, \"sheet\": \"Sheet1\"}, {\"cell\": \"A14\", \"value\": null, \"sheet\": \"Sheet1\"}, {\"cell\": \"A15\", \"value\": null, \"sheet\": \"Sheet1\"}]}", "sample_idx": 4, "latency_s": 11.1, "in_tokens": 838, "out_tokens": 509}
{"id": "279-23", "kind": "sheet-level", "path": "codegen-readback", "system": "You write self-contained Python that edits a workbook with openpyxl ONLY. No torch, no network, no pip install, no os/sys/subprocess/pathlib. INIT_XLSX and OUT_XLSX are already defined as path strings. Load INIT_XLSX, compute the answer from the real workbook (not the preview), write the graded answer cells, save to OUT_XLSX. Print exactly one line: SUMMARY_JSON={\"status\": \"ok|error\", \"notes\": \"...\"}. Never fabricate numbers — compute them from the workbook. Allowed imports: openpyxl, datetime, math, json, re, statistics, collections, itertools, copy, decimal.", "prompt": "## Instruction\nIncorporate a formula that deletes everything outside of parentheses into a VBA macro or which iterates over all cells in column B without gaps. Display results in Column B. Leave blank cells blank, especially do not paste 0 into blank cells. If there are no parentheses, leave the cell as is.\n\n## Workbook (preview — read INIT_XLSX for full data)\n### Sheet: Sheet1 (showing 26x2 of 26x2)\n\tA\tB\n1\t\t\n2\t\t\n3\t1\t(tig) this is good\n4\t2\t(tig) this is good\n5\t3\t(tib) this is bad\n6\t4\t(tig) this is good\n7\t5\t(tig) this is good\n8\t6\t(tib) this is bad\n9\t7\t(tig) this is good\n10\t8\t(tig) this is good\n11\t9\t(tib) this is bad\n12\t10\t(tig) this is good\n13\t\t\n14\t\t\n15\t\t\n16\t\t\n17\t1\ttig\n18\t2\ttig\n19\t3\ttib\n20\t4\ttig\n21\t5\ttig\n22\t6\ttib\n23\t7\ttig\n24\t8\ttig\n25\t9\ttib\n26\t10\ttig\n\n### Answer range (pinned, 48 cells)\nSheet1!A3=1\nSheet1!B3=(tig) this is good\nSheet1!A4=2\nSheet1!B4=(tig) this is good\nSheet1!A5=3\nSheet1!B5=(tib) this is bad\nSheet1!A6=4\nSheet1!B6=(tig) this is good\nSheet1!A7=5\nSheet1!B7=(tig) this is good\nSheet1!A8=6\nSheet1!B8=(tib) this is bad\nSheet1!A9=7\nSheet1!B9=(tig) this is good\nSheet1!A10=8\nSheet1!B10=(tig) this is good\nSheet1!A11=9\nSheet1!B11=(tib) this is bad\nSheet1!A12=10\nSheet1!B12=(tig) this is good\nSheet1!A13=\nSh