{"id": "297-42", "kind": "sheet-level", "path": "codegen-readback", "system": "You write self-contained Python that edits a workbook with openpyxl ONLY. No torch, no network, no pip install, no os/sys/subprocess/pathlib. INIT_XLSX and OUT_XLSX are already defined as path strings. Load INIT_XLSX, compute the answer from the real workbook (not the preview), write the graded answer cells, save to OUT_XLSX. Print exactly one line: SUMMARY_JSON={\"status\": \"ok|error\", \"notes\": \"...\"}. Never fabricate numbers — compute them from the workbook. Allowed imports: openpyxl, datetime, math, json, re, statistics, collections, itertools, copy, decimal.", "prompt": "## Instruction\nRunning my macro only creates a new sheet named 'combined' without pulling in the data from the other sheets. Use a macro or similar function to copy the data from the existing sheets into the newly created 'combined' sheet. I have given the header of the expected output in the 'combined sheet' in the attachment. Please start from cell A2 to output the answer, pay attention to the position, mapping between the answer and the header name.\n\n## Workbook (preview — read INIT_XLSX for full data)\n### Sheet: combined (showing 1x15 of 1x15)\n\tA\tB\tC\tD\tE\tF\tG\tH\tI\tJ\tK\tL\tM\tN\tO\n1\tFull Name\tHire Date\tHire Month\tCity\tProvince\tEmployment type\tYears\tBase Salary\tBonus\tOvertime\tCommission\tTotal Compensation\tDepartment\tPTO Days\tSick Days\n\n### Sheet: sindh (showing 120x15 of 324x15)\n\tA\tB\tC\tD\tE\tF\tG\tH\tI\tJ\tK\tL\tM\tN\tO\n1\tFull Name\tHire Date\tHire Month\tCity\tProvince\tEmployment type\tYears\tBase Salary\tBonus\tOvertime\tCommission\tTotal Compensation\tDepartment\tPTO Days\tSick Days\n2\tFatima\t42794\t42794\tKarachi\tSindh\tFull-time\t42794\t161713\t24257\t16171\t16171\t185970\tMarketing\t11\t4\n3\tAsma\t43187\t43187\tKarachi\tSindh\tFull-time\t43187\t185574\t27836\t18557\t18557\t213410\tAdministration\t11\t4\n4\tAbbas\t43028\t43028\tHyderabad\tSindh\tFull-time\t43028