\"cell\": \"I700\", \"value\": 759.1500000000001, \"sheet\": \"Sheet1\"}, {\"cell\": \"J700\", \"value\": 4301.85, \"sheet\": \"Sheet1\"}, {\"cell\": \"K700\", \"value\": 3615, \"sheet\": \"Sheet1\"}, {\"cell\": \"L700\", \"value\": 686.8500000000001, \"sheet\": \"Sheet1\"}, {\"cell\": \"M700\", \"value\": \"2014-04-01T00:00:00\", \"sheet\": \"Sheet1\"}, {\"cell\": \"N700\", \"value\": 4, \"sheet\": \"Sheet1\"}, {\"cell\": \"O700\", \"value\": \"April\", \"sheet\": \"Sheet1\"}, {\"cell\": \"P700\", \"value\": \"2014\", \"sheet\": \"Sheet1\"}, {\"cell\": \"Q700\", \"value\": null, \"sheet\": \"Sheet1\"}, {\"cell\": \"A701\", \"value\": \"Channel Partners\", \"sheet\": \"Sheet1\"}, {\"cell\": \"B701\", \"value\": \"United States of America\", \"sheet\": \"Sheet1\"}, {\"cell\": \"C701\", \"value\": \"VTT\", \"sheet\": \"Sheet1\"}, {\"cell\": \"D701\", \"value\": \"High\", \"sheet\": \"Sheet1\"}, {\"cell\": \"E701\", \"value\": 1806, \"sheet\": \"Sheet1\"}, {\"cell\": \"F701\", \"value\": 250, \"sheet\": \"Sheet1\"}, {\"cell\": \"G701\", \"value\": 12, \"sheet\": \"Sheet1\"}, {\"cell\": \"H701\", \"value\": 21672, \"sheet\": \"Sheet1\"}, {\"cell\": \"I701\", \"value\": 3250.8, \"sheet\": \"Sheet1\"}, {\"cell\": \"J701\", \"value\": 18421.2, \"sheet\": \"Sheet1\"}, {\"cell\": \"K701\", \"value\": 5418, \"sheet\": \"Sheet1\"}, {\"cell\": \"L701\", \"value\": 13003.2, \"sheet\": \"Sheet1\"}, {\"cell\": \"M701\", \"value\": \"2014-05-01T00:00:00\", \"sheet\": \"Sheet1\"}, {\"cell\": \"N701\", \"value\": 5, \"sheet\": \"Sheet1\"}, {\"cell\": \"O701\", \"value\": \"May\", \"sheet\": \"Sheet1\"}, {\"cell\": \"P701\", \"value\": \"2014\", \"sheet\": \"Sheet1\"}, {\"cell\": \"Q701\", \"value\": null, \"sheet\": \"Sheet1\"}]}", "sample_idx": 2, "latency_s": 10.4, "in_tokens": 13512, "out_tokens": 251}
{"id": "384-4", "kind": "sheet-level", "path": "codegen-readback", "system": "You write self-contained Python that edits a workbook with openpyxl ONLY. No torch, no network, no pip install, no os/sys/subprocess/pathlib. INIT_XLSX and OUT_XLSX are already defined as path strings. Load INIT_XLSX, compute the answer from the real workbook (not the preview), write the graded answer cells, save to OUT_XLSX. Print exactly one line: SUMMARY_JSON={\"status\": \"ok|error\", \"notes\": \"...\"}. Never fabricate numbers — compute them from the workbook. Allowed imports: openpyxl, datetime, math, json, re, statistics, collections, itertools, copy, decimal.", "prompt": "## Instruction\nHow can I use VBA to determine the differences in values between two data sources in Excel? Please copy values that appear in the 'Source' table, but not in the 'Source2' table, to the 'Result' table, unless the value is 2. If the value '2' is present in both sources, include it in the 'Result' table. Make sure to include it only once.\n\n## Workbook (preview — read INIT_XLSX for full data)\n### Sheet: Source (showing 8x2 of 8x2)\n\tA\tB\n1\tItem\tValue\n2\tA\t1\n3\tA\t2\n4\tB\t2\n5\tD\t3\n6\tC\t3\n7\tA\t4\n8\tB\t5\n\n### Sheet: Source2 (showing 5x1 of 5x1)\n\tA\n1\tValue\n2\t1\n3\t2\n4\t3\n5\t3\n\n### Sheet: Result (showing 1x1 of 1x1)\n\tA\n1\tValue\n\n### Answer range (pinned, 7 cells)\nResult!A2=\nResult!A3=\nResult!A4=\nResult!A5=\nResult!A6=\nResult!A7=\nResult!A8=\n\n## Answer range\nSheet: Result\nCells: Result'!A2:A8\nData range: Source!A1:B8','Source2!A1:B8','Result!A1:B8'\nGraded cells: Result!A2, Result!A3, Result!A4, Result!A5, Result!A6, Result!A7, Result!A8\n\n\n## Skill\n### Skill: sheet reorganization\n- Never run/emit VBA or macros; implement the equivalent Python transform on the sheets.\n- When deleting rows, iterate bottom-up so indices stay valid; preserve the header row and any rows above it unless told otherwise.\n- Keep sheet names byte-exact (quotes/spaces matter). Do not create helper sheets or write outside the requested target range.\n\n### Skill: writing cells\n- Write computed VALUES (not formulas) unless the task explicitly requires formula text.\n- Write every requested answer cell; an unwritten cell scores zero. Convert Python types to plain scalars (no numpy types, no datetime objects — use ISO strings).\n\n\nReply with a single Python script in a ```python fence. No prose. INIT_XLSX and OUT_XLSX are predefined. Save OUT_XLSX and print one SUMMARY_JSON line.", "completion": "{\"cells\": [{\"cell\": \"A2\", \"value\": 2, \"sheet\": \"Result\"}, {\"cell\": \"A3\", \"value\": 4, \"sheet\": \"Result\"}, {\"cell\": \"A4\", \"value\": 5, \"sheet\": \"Result\"}, {\"cell\": \"A5\", \"value\": null, \"sheet\": \"Result\"}, {\"cell\": \"A6\", \"value\": null, \"sheet\": \"Result\"}, {\"cell\": \"A7\", \"value\": null, \"sheet\": \"Result\"}, {\"cell\": \"A8\", \"value\": null, \"sheet\": \"Result\"}]}", "sample_idx": 5, "latency_s": 10.0, "in_tokens": 698, "out_tokens": 455}
{"id": "408-5", "kind": "sheet-level", "path": "codegen-readback", "system": "You write self-contained Python that edits a workbook with openpyxl ONLY. No torch, no network, no pip install, no os/sys/subprocess/pathlib. INIT_XLSX and OUT_XLSX are already defined as path strings. Load INIT_XLSX, compute the answer from the real workbook (not the preview), write the graded answer cells, save to OUT_XLSX. Print exactly one line: SUMMARY_JSON={\"status\": \"ok|error\", \"notes\": \"...\"}. Never fabricate numbers — compute them from the workbook. Allowed imports: openpyxl, datetime, math, json, re, statistics, collections, itertools, copy, decimal.", "prompt": "## Instruction\nHow can I create a macro in Excel to calculate the sum of values in Column D for rows where Column E contains a zero, insert this result into Column D next to the row containing 'BR1 Sales' in Column C, and then delete all rows where Column E contains a zero except for the rows where the reference contains 'BR1 Sales'? Also delete blank lines. If Macro is not possible, just perform this task.\n\n## Workbook (preview — read INIT_XLSX for full data)\n### Sheet: Sheet1 (showing 120x5 of 137x5)\n\tA\tB\tC\tD\tE\n1\tDate\tBranch\tReference\tAmount\tMatch Ref and Val\n2\t2021-06-01 00:00:00\tBR1 PL\t968390\t-48.36\t0\n3\t2021-06-01 00:00:00\tBR1 PL\t968388\t-791.2\t0\n4\t2021-06-01 00:00:00\tBR1 PL\t968388\t-587.37\t0\n5\t2021-06-01 00:00:00\tBR1 PL\t968390\t-5009.88\t0\n6\t2021-06-02 00:00:00\tBR1 PL\t968392\t-1008.77\t0\n7\t2021-06-02 00:00:00\tBR1 PL\t968391\t-60.01\t0\n8\t2021-06-02 00:00:00\tBR1 PL\t968391\t-1303.14\t0\n9\t2021-06-02 00:00:00\tBR1 PL\t968391\t-2613.55\t0\n10\t2021-06-02 00:00:00\tBR1 PL\t968393\t-644.42\t0\n11\t2021-06-02 00:00:00\tBR1 PL\t968391\t-30.51\t0\n12\t2021-06-03 00:00:00\tBR1 PL\t968395\t-1108.38\t0\n13\t2021-06-03 00:00:00\tBR1 PL\t968395\t-43.14\t0\n14\t2021-06-03 00:00:00\tBR1 PL\t968395\t-73.41\t0\n15\t2021-06-03 00:00:00\tBR1 PL\t968393\t-1782.79\t0\n16\t2021-06-04 