=\nNumbers!A8=\nNumbers!B8=\nNumbers!C8=\nNumbers!D8=\nNumbers!E8=\nNumbers!F8=\nNumbers!A9=\nNumbers!B9=\nNumbers!C9=\nNumbers!D9=\nNumbers!E9=\nNumbers!F9=\n\n## Answer range\nSheet: Numbers\nCells: 'Numbers'!A1:F9\nData range: Raw Data!'A1:F18, 'Manual Result!'A1:F9\nGraded cells: Numbers!A1, Numbers!B1, Numbers!C1, Numbers!D1, Numbers!E1, Numbers!F1, Numbers!A2, Numbers!B2, Numbers!C2, Numbers!D2, Numbers!E2, Numbers!F2, Numbers!A3, Numbers!B3, Numbers!C3, Numbers!D3, Numbers!E3, Numbers!F3, Numbers!A4, Numbers!B4, Numbers!C4, Numbers!D4, Numbers!E4, Numbers!F4, Numbers!A5, Numbers!B5, Numbers!C5, Numbers!D5, Numbers!E5, Numbers!F5, Numbers!A6, Numbers!B6, Numbers!C6, Numbers!D6, Numbers!E6, Numbers!F6, Numbers!A7, Numbers!B7, Numbers!C7, Numbers!D7, Numbers!E7, Numbers!F7, Numbers!A8, Numbers!B8, Numbers!C8, Numbers!D8, Numbers!E8, Numbers!F8, Numbers!A9, Numbers!B9, Numbers!C9, Numbers!D9, Numbers!E9, Numbers!F9\n\n\n## Skill\n### Skill: sheet reorganization\n- Never run/emit VBA or macros; implement the equivalent Python transform on the sheets.\n- When deleting rows, iterate bottom-up so indices stay valid; preserve the header row and any rows above it unless told otherwise.\n- Keep sheet names byte-exact (quotes/spaces matter). Do not create helper sheets or write outside the requested target range.\n\n### Skill: writing cells\n- Write computed VALUES (not formulas) unless the task explicitly requires formula text.\n- Write every requested answer cell; an unwritten cell scores zero. Convert Python types to plain scalars (no numpy types, no datetime objects — use ISO strings).\n\n\nReply with a single Python script in a ```python fence. No prose. INIT_XLSX and OUT_XLSX are predefined. Save OUT_XLSX and print one SUMMARY_JSON line.", "completion": "{\"cells\": [{\"cell\": \"A1\", \"value\": 12, \"sheet\": \"Numbers\"}, {\"cell\": \"B1\", \"value\": 19, \"sheet\": \"Numbers\"}, {\"cell\": \"C1\", \"value\": 18, \"sheet\": \"Numbers\"}, {\"cell\": \"D1\", \"val