{"id": "84-40", "kind": "sheet-level", "path": "codegen-readback", "system": "You write self-contained Python that edits a workbook with openpyxl ONLY. No torch, no network, no pip install, no os/sys/subprocess/pathlib. INIT_XLSX and OUT_XLSX are already defined as path strings. Load INIT_XLSX, compute the answer from the real workbook (not the preview), write the graded answer cells, save to OUT_XLSX. Print exactly one line: SUMMARY_JSON={\"status\": \"ok|error\", \"notes\": \"...\"}. Never fabricate numbers — compute them from the workbook. Allowed imports: openpyxl, datetime, math, json, re, statistics, collections, itertools, copy, decimal.", "prompt": "## Instruction\nI need to sum the amounts in the entire columns C and D for each sheet, excluding column B, in an Excel workbook. These sums should then be populated in a 'list' sheet, putting the names of the sheets into column B. For each sheet, column C in list tab should contain the total from the original sheet's column C, and column D in list tab should contain the total from the original sheet's column D. Additionally, column E in the 'list' sheet should show the result of subtracting the amount in column D from the amount in column C. I also want a total row at the end that sums the amounts from all these sheets. Whenever I add new sheets before the 'list' sheet, I need the existing data in the 'list' sheet to be cleared so that the list can be updated to reflect any changes in the other sheets. I've provided an attachment for reference.\n\n## Workbook (preview — read INIT_XLSX for full data)\n### Sheet: CA (showing 17x5 of 17x5)\n\tA\tB\tC\tD\tE\n1\tDATE\tBATCH\tIMPORT\tEXPORT\t\n2\t2023-01-01 00:00:00\tSTR\t2000\t\t\n3\t2023-01-02 00:00:00\tSTR1\t2200\t\t\n4\t2023-01-03 00:00:00\tMMNR\t2400\t1200\t\n5\t2023-01-04 00:00:00\tMMDT\t2600\t1300\t\n6\t2023-01-05 00:00:00\tMSR\t2800\t1400\t\n7\t2023-01-06 00:00:00\tSTR\t\t1500\t\n8\t2023-01-07 00:00:00\tSTR1\t\t1600\t\n9\t2023-01-08 00:00:00\tSTR\t\t1700\t\n10\t2023-02-09 00:00:00\tMMDT\t\t1800\t\n11\t2023-02-10 00:00:00\tMSR\t3800\t\t\n12\t2023-02-11 00:00:00\tSTR\t4000\t2000\t\n13\t2023-02-12 00:00:00\tSTR1\t4200\t2100\t\n14\t2023-02-13 00:00:00\tMMNR\t4400\t\t\n15\t2023-02-14 00:00:00\tMMDT\t4400\t\t\n16\t2023-02-15 00:00:00\tMSR\t4400\t2200\t\n17\t\t\t\t\t\n\n### Sheet: MN (showing 17x4 of 17x4)\n\tA\tB\tC\tD\n1\tDATE\tBATCH\tIMPORT\tEXPORT\n2\t2023-01-01 00:00:00\tSER4\t\t400\n3\t2023-01-02 00:00:00\tSER5\t\t500\n4\t2023-01-03 00:00:00\tSER6\t1000\t400\n5\t2023-01-04 00:00:00\tMMDRNM\t6000\t1300\n6\t2023-01-05 00:00:00\tMSRMAQ\t500\t\n7\t2023-01-06 00:00:00\tSTR13\t\t1500\n8\t2023-01-07 00:00:00\tSTR14\t\t1600\n9\t2023-01-08 00:00:00\tSTR15\t\t1700\n10\t2023-02-09 00:00:00\tSTR16\t\t1800\n11\t2023-02-10 00:00:00\tSTR17\t500\t\n12\t2023-02-11 00:00:00\tSTR18\t900\t600\n13\t2023-02-12 00:00:00\tSTR19\t6000\t\n14\t2023-02-13 00:00:00\tSTR20\t5000\t\n15\t2023-02-14 00:00:00\tSTR21\t2000\t\n16\t2023-02-15 00:00:00\tSTR22\t4400\t2200\n17\t\t\t\t\n\n### Sheet: SDFRT (showing 7x4 of 7x4)\n\tA\tB\tC\tD\n1\tDATE\tBATCH\tIMPORT\tEXPORT\n2\t2023-01-01 00:00:00\tSER41\t7000\t\n3\t2023-01-02 00:00:00\tSER42\t8000\t\n4\t2023-01-03 00:00:00\tSER43\t5000\t400\n5\t2023-01-04 00:00:00\tMMDRQW2\t6000\t\n6\t2023-01-05 00:00:00\tMMDRQW3\t500\t400\n7\t\t\t\t\n\n### Sheet: LIST (showing 5x5 of 5x5)\n\tA\tB\tC\tD\tE\n1\tITEMS\tSHEETS NAMES\tIMPORT\tEXPORT\tBALANCE\n2\t1\tCA\t37200\t16800\t20400\n3\t2\tMN\t26300\t12000\t14300\n4\t3\tSDFRT\t\t\t\n5\t\tTOTAL\t\t\t\n\n### Answer range (pinned, 12 cells)\nLIST!C2=37200\nLIST!D2=16800\nLIST!E2=20400\nLIST!C3=26300\nLIST!D3=12000\nLIST!E3=14300\nLIST!C4=\nLIST!D4=\nLIST!E4=\nLIST!C5=\nLIST!D5=\nLIST!E5=\n\n## Answer range\nSheet: LIST\nCells: 'LIST'!C2:E5\nData range: CA!'A1:D16,'MN!'A1:D16,'SDFRT!'A1:D6,'LIST!'A1:E6\nGraded cells: LIST!C2, LIST!D2, LIST!E2, LIST!C3, LIST!D3, LIST!E3, LIST!C4, LIST!D4, LIST!E4, LIST!C5, LIST!D5, LIST!E5\n\n\n## Skill\n### Skill: date arithmetic\n- Parse dates with datetime (try common formats); keep them as datetime objects, never strings, until the final write.\n- Day differences are (a - b).days on dates; respect inclusive/exclusive wording in the instruction. Output dates as YYYY-MM-DD (or YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS if times are involved).\n\n### Skill: writing cells\n- Write computed VALUES (not formulas) unless the task explicitly requires formula text.\n- Write every requested answer cell; an unwritten cell scores zero. Convert Python types to plain scalars (no numpy types, no datetime objects — use ISO strings).\n\n\nReply with a single Python script in a ```python fence. No prose. INIT_XLSX and OUT_XLSX are predefined. Save OUT_XLSX and print one SUMMARY_JSON line.", "completion": "{\"cells\": [{\"cell\": \"C2\", \"value\": 37200, \"sheet\": \"LIST\"}, {\"cell\": \"D2\", \"value\": 16800, \"sheet\": \"LIST\"}, {\"cell\": \"E2\", \"value\": 20400, \"sheet\": \"LIST\"}, {\"cell\": \"C3\", \"value\": 26300, \"sheet\": \"LIST\"}, {\"cell\": \"D3\", \"value\": 12000, \"sheet\": \"LIST\"}, {\"cell\": \"E3\", \"value\": 14300, \"sheet\": \"LIST\"}, {\"cell\": \"C4\", \"value\": 26500, \"sheet\": \"LIST\"}, {\"cell\": \"D4\", \"value\": 800, \"sheet\": \"LIST\"}, {\"cell\": \"E4\", \"value\": 25700, \"sheet\": \"LIST\"}, {\"cell\": \"C5\", \"value\": 90000, \"sheet\": \"LIST\"}, {\"cell\": \"D5\", \"value\": 29600, \"sheet\": \"LIST\"}, {\"cell\": \"E5\", \"value\": 60400, \"sheet\": \"LIST\"}]}", "sample_idx": 4, "latency_s": 11.6, "in_tokens": 2125, "out_tokens": 681}
{"id": "91-34", "kind": "sheet-level", "path": "codegen-readback", "system": "You write self-contained Python that edits a workbook with openpyxl ONLY. No torch, no network, no pip install, no os/sys/subprocess/pathlib. INIT_XLSX and OUT_XLSX are already defined as path strings. Load INIT_XLSX, compute the answer from the real workbook (not the preview), write the graded answer cells, save to OUT_XLSX. Print exactly one line: SUMMARY_JSON={\"status\": \"ok|error\", \"notes\": \"...\"}. Never fabricate numbers — compute them from the workbook. Allowed imports: openpyxl, datetime, math, json, re, statistics, collections, itertools, copy, decimal.", "prompt": "## Instruction\nCreate a macro or Delete only one entry of a person (same last name, first name, and DOB) marked 'Yes' in the 'Duplicate?' column, provided that the 'Relationship' column for these duplicates is anything but 'Employee'? For example, Emily Doees is listed twice as non-employee, so one entry should be deleted, but Lisa Doees, present as both a spouse and an employee, should not have either entry deleted.\n\n## Workbook (preview — read INIT_XLSX for full data)\n### Sheet: SwiftMD (showing 42x15 of 42x15)\n\tA\tB\tC\tD\tE\tF\tG\tH\tI\tJ\tK\tL\tM\tN\tO\n1\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n2\t\tSSN\tLast Name\tFirst Name\tGender\tDate Of Birth\tDuplicate?\tRelationship\tAddress\tCity\tState\tZip\tEmployee #\tMarital Status\tPhone #\n3\t\t\tDue\tJohn\tMale\t2002-04-11 00:00:00\tNo\tEmployee\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n4\t\t\tDame\tJane\tFemale\t1998-07-18 00:00:00\tNo\tEmployee\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n5\t\t\tRattice\tMatrha\tFemale\t1983-08-11 00:00:00\tNo\tEmployee\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n6\t\t\tSmith\tAntoinette\tFemale\t1967-05-21 00:00:00\tYes\tEmployee\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n7\t\t\tSmith\tAntoinette\tFemale\t1967-05-21 00:00:00\tYes\tSpouse\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n8\t\t\tMoon\tJustice\tFemale\t2002-01-10 00:00:00\tYes\tChild living at home\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n9\t\t\tMoon\tJustice\tFemale\t2002-01-10 00:00:00\tYes\tEmployee\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n10\t\t\tAmerica\