{"id": "118-50", "kind": "sheet-level", "path": "codegen-readback", "system": "You write self-contained Python that edits a workbook with openpyxl ONLY. No torch, no network, no pip install, no os/sys/subprocess/pathlib. INIT_XLSX and OUT_XLSX are already defined as path strings. Load INIT_XLSX, compute the answer from the real workbook (not the preview), write the graded answer cells, save to OUT_XLSX. Print exactly one line: SUMMARY_JSON={\"status\": \"ok|error\", \"notes\": \"...\"}. Never fabricate numbers — compute them from the workbook. Allowed imports: openpyxl, datetime, math, json, re, statistics, collections, itertools, copy, decimal.", "prompt": "## Instruction\nSort the names in column A in alphabetical order. I need a macro to find words in an Excel file with a specified pattern where the last three letters of a word, such as 'PEA' in 'EARTHPEA', are the same. Additionally, for a match, the fifth letter should become the first letter, as in transforming 'EARTHPEA' to 'HEARTPEA'. The Excel file contains a list of words within 5000 rows, and the macro should be able to search through 55,555 rows to present the results. The results should be pasted in pairs at columns C and D. The original words should be in column D and the transformations should be in column C. Group results based on their endings and sort them in the following order: ING, ERS, ATE, EST, ONE, IER, ILY. Do not add any extra headings or formatting to Sheet1.\n\n## Workbook (preview — read INIT_XLSX for full data)\n### Sheet: Sheet1 (showing 120x4 of 5000x4)\n\tA\tB\tC\tD\n1\tAROINTED\t\tEARTHPEA\tHEARTPEA\n2\tDERATION\t\t\t\n3\tORDINATE\t\t\t\n4\tRATIONED\t\t\t\n5\tORIENTAL\t\t\t\n6\tRELATION\t\t\t\n7\tTAILERON\t\t\t\n8\tANOESTRI\t\t\t\n9\tARSONITE\t\t\t\n10\tNOTAIRES\t\t\t\n11\tNOTARIES\t\t\t\n12\tNOTARISE\t\t\t\n13\tROSINATE\t\t\t\n14\tSENORITA\t\t\t\n15\tAERATION\t\t\t\n16\tAEROLITE\t\t\t\n17\tETAERIOS\t\t\t\n18\tDELATION\t\t\t\n19\tIDOLATER\t\t\t\n20\tTAILORED\t\t\t\n21\tANEROIDS\t\t\