{"id": "168-17", "kind": "sheet-level", "path": "codegen-readback", "system": "You write self-contained Python that edits a workbook with openpyxl ONLY. No torch, no network, no pip install, no os/sys/subprocess/pathlib. INIT_XLSX and OUT_XLSX are already defined as path strings. Load INIT_XLSX, compute the answer from the real workbook (not the preview), write the graded answer cells, save to OUT_XLSX. Print exactly one line: SUMMARY_JSON={\"status\": \"ok|error\", \"notes\": \"...\"}. Never fabricate numbers — compute them from the workbook. Allowed imports: openpyxl, datetime, math, json, re, statistics, collections, itertools, copy, decimal.", "prompt": "## Instruction\nHow can I write a macro in Excel to locate the first instance of 'Invoice No.' in column A on the 'Statement' sheet and delete all preceding rows, ensuring that the first instance of 'Invoice No.' appears in cell A1 after running the macro?\n\n## Workbook (preview — read INIT_XLSX for full data)\n### Sheet: Statement (showing 12x5 of 12x5)\n\tA\tB\tC\tD\tE\n1\t\t\t\t\t\n2\t\tSALES AND ACCESSORIES\t\t\t\n3\t\tACCOUNT STATEMENT\t\t\t\n4\tAccount Number: KRT821476\tBR1 Ltd\t\t\t\n5\tBR1 Southern Area\t28 Victoria Link\t\t\t\n6\tPO  996314XC\t\t\t\t\n7\tCaldon\t X30\tDate: 02.11.2022\t\t\n8\t881765\t\t\t\t\n9\t\t\tAccount Contact: Steve Caldwell\t\t\n10\t\t\tPhone:\t\t\n11\tThe currency on this statement is Dollars\t\tE-mail: Steve.Caldwell@Br1.com\t\t\n12\tInvoice No.\tTransaction Date\tDue Date\tDescription\tAmount\n\n### Sheet: Final result (showing 1x5 of 1x5)\n\tA\tB\tC\tD\tE\n1\tInvoice No.\tTransaction Date\tDue Date\tDescription\tAmount\n\n### Answer range (pinned, 55 cells)\nStatement!A2=\nStatement!B2=SALES AND ACCESSORIES\nStatement!C2=\nStatement!D2=\nStatement!E2=\nStatement!A3=\nStatement!B3=ACCOUNT STATEMENT\nStatement!C3=\nStatement!D3=\nStatement!E3=\nStatement!A4=Account Number: KRT821476\nStatement!B4=BR1 Ltd\nStatement!C4=\nStatement!D4=\nStatement!E4=\nStatement!A5=BR1 Southern A