{"id": "170-13", "kind": "sheet-level", "path": "codegen-readback", "system": "You write self-contained Python that edits a workbook with openpyxl ONLY. No torch, no network, no pip install, no os/sys/subprocess/pathlib. INIT_XLSX and OUT_XLSX are already defined as path strings. Load INIT_XLSX, compute the answer from the real workbook (not the preview), write the graded answer cells, save to OUT_XLSX. Print exactly one line: SUMMARY_JSON={\"status\": \"ok|error\", \"notes\": \"...\"}. Never fabricate numbers — compute them from the workbook. Allowed imports: openpyxl, datetime, math, json, re, statistics, collections, itertools, copy, decimal.", "prompt": "## Instruction\nHow can I check if a header from Sheet2 exists in the Entry column of Sheet1, and if it does, insert the same number of rows as there are in Sheet2 for that header? After insertion, I want to append the data from the matching row in Sheet1 and copy over the associated data from Sheet2 into Sheet3 under a column named 'Output'. If a header from Sheet2 does not have a corresponding entry in Sheet1, it should be ignored. An example is provided where 'Sheet2 Header - U4_ComponentPropertyForm' has various associated data that needs to be matched with a similarly titled header in Sheet1, then the process of row insertion and data appending should be repeated for each Sheet1 entry into Sheet3 till the last row of Sheet1.\n\n## Workbook (preview — read INIT_XLSX for full data)\n### Sheet: Sheet1 (showing 14x1 of 14x1)\n\tA\n1\tEntry\n2\tZPAM_FLEXI+U4_PackageDetailsRelation+U4_PackageDetailsForm+Sealing Method+\n3\tZPAM_FLEXI+U4_CompPropertyRelation+U4_ComponentPropertyForm+Solvent Retention_including Ethanol+\n4\tZPAM_FLEXI+U4_CompPropertyRelation+U4_ComponentPropertyForm+Hot Tack Strength_N/45mm+\n5\tZPAM_FLEXI+U4_CompPropertyRelation+U4_VisualPerformanceForm+Block+\n6\tZPAM_FLEXI+U4_PackageDetailsRelation+U4_PackageDetailsForm+Form+\n7\tZPAM_FLEXI+U4_PackageDetailsRelation+U4_PackageDetailsForm+Surface