{"id": "254-34", "kind": "sheet-level", "path": "codegen-readback", "system": "You write self-contained Python that edits a workbook with openpyxl ONLY. No torch, no network, no pip install, no os/sys/subprocess/pathlib. INIT_XLSX and OUT_XLSX are already defined as path strings. Load INIT_XLSX, compute the answer from the real workbook (not the preview), write the graded answer cells, save to OUT_XLSX. Print exactly one line: SUMMARY_JSON={\"status\": \"ok|error\", \"notes\": \"...\"}. Never fabricate numbers — compute them from the workbook. Allowed imports: openpyxl, datetime, math, json, re, statistics, collections, itertools, copy, decimal.", "prompt": "## Instruction\nI've provided a spreadsheet with a 'before' and 'after' sheet. In the 'before' sheet, some values are colored green, and these specific values sum up to amounts between 994108 and 994112. I manually highlighted these values, but how can I automate this process through VBA code to highlight the cells that, when combined, provide a specific sum? Alternatively, if it's more appropriate, could you solve this using conditional formatting? I'm also curious about how to handle multiple combinations of values that could result in the sums specified. Please delete Sheet3 and make certain the highlighted cells on the \"Before\" Sheet are color: #00FF00. Put the one valid combination numerical value in cell C2.\n\n## Workbook (preview — read INIT_XLSX for full data)\n### Sheet: Before (showing 16x1 of 16x1)\n\tA\n1\t22704\n2\t345510\n3\t1238917\n4\t30424.000000000004\n5\t564077.969\n6\t406152.99999999994\n7\t60073\n8\t436880\n9\t158419\n10\t277936.04750000004\n11\t293976\n12\t827362\n13\t342830\n14\t146354\n15\t1146945\n16\t230626\n\n### Sheet: After (showing 16x1 of 16x1)\n\tA\n1\t22704\n2\t345510\n3\t1238917\n4\t30424.000000000004\n5\t564077.969\n6\t406152.99999999994\n7\t60073\n8\t436880\n9\t158419\n10\t277936.04750000004\n11\t293976\n12\t827362\n13\t342830\n14\t146354\n15\t1146945\n16\t230626\n\n### Sheet: Sheet3 (showing 1x1 of 1x1)\n\tA\n1\t\n\n### Sheet: After highlighted cells: A1=FF00B0F0, A2=FF00B0F0, A4=FF00B0F0, A7=FF00B0F0, A9=FF00B0F0, A14=FF00B0F0, A16=FF00B0F0\n\n### Answer range (pinned, 1 cells)\nBefore!C2=\n\n## Answer range\nSheet: Before\nCells: 'Before'!C2\nData range: A1:A16\nGraded cells: Before!C2\n\n\n## Skill\n### Skill: sheet reorganization\n- Never run/emit VBA or macros; implement the equivalent Python transform on the sheets.\n- When deleting rows, iterate bottom-up so indices stay valid; preserve the header row and any rows above it unless told otherwise.\n- Keep sheet names byte-exact (quotes/spaces matter). Do not create helper sheets or write outside the requested target range.\n\n### Skill: formatting-gated logic\n- The instruction gates on cell appearance (highlight/fill/color). Read each cell's fill color (openpyxl `cell.fill.start_color.rgb`) and apply the transform ONLY to cells whose fill matches the stated color.\n\n\nReply with a single Python script in a ```python fence. No prose. INIT_XLSX and OUT_XLSX are predefined. Save OUT_XLSX and print one SUMMARY_JSON line.", "completion": "{\"cells\": [{\"cell\": \"C2\", \"value\": 994110, \"sheet\": \"Before\"}]}", "sample_idx": 4, "latency_s": 15.8, "in_tokens": 1096, "out_tokens": 924}
{"id": "108-24", "kind": "sheet-level", "path": "codegen-readback", "system": "You write self-contained Python that edits a workbook with openpyxl ONLY. No torch, no network, no pip install, no os/sys/subprocess/pathlib. INIT_XLSX and OUT_XLSX are already defined as path strings. Load INIT_XLSX, compute the answer from the real workbook (not the preview), write the graded answer cells, save to OUT_XLSX. Print exactly one line: SUMMARY_JSON={\"status\": \"ok|error\", \"notes\": \"...\"}. Never fabricate numbers — compute them from the workbook. Allowed imports: openpyxl, datetime, math, json, re, statistics, collections, itertools, copy, decimal.", "prompt": "## Instruction\nHow can I create a macro to extract rows from sheet 'BZTB', where descriptions in column B start with 'COS Pass，COS Comm，COS W/S' and include the word 'Used'?   The relevant data from columns A to D should be pasted into sheet 'Tema UV COS' in columns A to D, starting from row 1. Exclude '398726' from your results.\n\n## Workbook (preview — read INIT_XLSX for full data)\n### Sheet: BZTB (showing 120x4 of 141x4)\n\tA\tB\tC\tD\n1\t398725\tSale Retail 28 CX 3 New\t-14863.3912\t-177880.6536\n2\t398726\tCOS Pass  - A Used\t347.826\t7239.808\n3\t398727\tFact Assist 28 CX 3 New\t-173.92\t-2347.9132\n4\t398728\tO/allowance 28 CX 3 New\t0\t790.8528\n5\t398729\tCOS 28 CX 3 - Base Cost New\t13196.7492\t160572.986\n6\t398730\tCOS 28 CX 3 - PDI/Recon New\t44.8792\t881.3691999999999\n7\t398731\tCOS 28 CX 3 - Giveaway & ass New\t0\t812.2328\n8\t398732\tCOS 28 CX 3 - Spotters New\t0\t53.36\n9\t398733\tCOS 28 CX 3 - Delivery New\t0\t0\n10\t398734\tCOS 28 CX 3 - Jnls/adj/depr New\t38\t456\n11\t398735\tSale Retail 28 2 New\t-11147.84\t-168681.7984\n12\t398736\tDiscount Retail 28 2 New\t347.826\t4258.054\n13\t398737\tFact Assist 28 2 New\t-189.96\t-2885.76\n14\t398738\tO/allowance 28 2 New\t0\t1746.6228\n15\t398739\tCOS 28 2 - Base Cost New\t10110.3824\t151448.7644\n16\t398740\tCOS 28 2 - PDI/Recon New\t67.9704\t111