{"id": "188-39", "kind": "sheet-level", "path": "codegen-readback", "system": "You write self-contained Python that edits a workbook with openpyxl ONLY. No torch, no network, no pip install, no os/sys/subprocess/pathlib. INIT_XLSX and OUT_XLSX are already defined as path strings. Load INIT_XLSX, compute the answer from the real workbook (not the preview), write the graded answer cells, save to OUT_XLSX. Print exactly one line: SUMMARY_JSON={\"status\": \"ok|error\", \"notes\": \"...\"}. Never fabricate numbers — compute them from the workbook. Allowed imports: openpyxl, datetime, math, json, re, statistics, collections, itertools, copy, decimal.", "prompt": "## Instruction\nHow can I update a result sheet in Excel to display the designation, contact details, and email of a person when their designation matches either 'Branch Manager' or 'Branch Credit Manager' for a given location, while marking cells with 'N/A' if the designation is different? The data to be matched comes from a main sheet containing fields such as name, contact number, mail ID, and designation. The result is required in a structured format where the person's name is listed against their location, accompanied by contact details and mail ID if the designation criteria is met.  Left align all outputed entries.\n\n## Workbook (preview — read INIT_XLSX for full data)\n### Sheet: main sheet (showing 12x5 of 12x5)\n\tA\tB\tC\tD\tE\n1\tLocation\tName of employee\tContact no\tMail id\tDesignation\n2\tAhmedabad\tShravani Chavan\t8160550797\tshravani@yahoo.com\tMIS Manager\n3\tKolkata\tVidhya Nalawade\t7768825777\tvidhyan@gmail.com\tBranch Manager\n4\tSecunderabad\tPriya Patil\t9592887766\tpriyapatil.k@gmail.com\tBranch Credit Manager\n5\tVijaywada\tRahul john\t9998931336\trahul.john@gmail.com\tBranch Sales Manager\n6\tLucknow\tAshok Pitroda\t9711784231\tashokpa@yahoo.co.in\tCustomer Retention Manager\n7\tBengaluru\tVivek Govekar\t9999143233\tvivekgovekar1@gmail.com\tBranch Manager\n8\tAlwar\tNagaraju Pokala\t9425493385\tnagarajup@yahoo.com\tBranch Manager\n9\tMysore\tSanjay Kumar\t9035957169\tsanjayk@yahoo.co.in\tBranch Collection Officer\n10\tChennai\tKrishna Kiran P\t9845267900\tkrishnap@gmail.com\tBranch Credit Manager\n11\tLudhiana\tMahalakshmi N\t9952425727\tmahalakshmi@yahoo.com\tSales Co-ordinator\n12\tJaipur\tHari Gunimini\t7522944799\tharigu.p@gmail.com\tBranch Credit Manager\n\n### Sheet: result (showing 12x4 of 12x4)\n\tA\tB\tC\tD\n1\tLocation\tDesignation\tContact no\tMail id\n2\tAhmedabad\t\t\t\n3\tKolkata\t\t\t\n4\tSecunderabad\t\t\t\n5\tVijaywada\t\t\t\n6\tLucknow\t\t\t\n7\tBengaluru\t\t\t\n8\tAlwar\t\t\t\n9\tMysore\t\t\t\n10\tChennai\t\t\t\n11\tLudhiana\t\t\t\n12\tJaipur\t\t\t\n\n### Answer range (pinned, 33 cells)\nresult!B2=\nresult!C2=\nresult!D2=\nresult!B3=\nresult!C3=\nresult!D3=\nresult!B4=\nresult!C4=\nresult!D4=\nresult!B5=\nresult!C5=\nresult!D5=\nresult!B6=\nresult!C6=\nresult!D6=\nresult!B7=\nresult!C7=\nresult!D7=\nresult!B8=\nresult!C8=\nresult!D8=\nresult!B9=\nresult!C9=\nresult!D9=\nresult!B10=\nresult!C10=\nresult!D10=\nresult!B11=\nresult!C11=\nresult!D11=\nresult!B12=\nresult!C12=\nresult!D12=\n\n## Answer range\nSheet: result\nCells: 'result'!B2:D12\nData range: main!'A1: E12, 'result!'A1: D12'\nGraded cells: result!B2, result!C2, result!D2, result!B3, result!C3, result!D3, result!B4, result!C4, result!D4, result!B5, result!C5, result!D5, result!B6, result!C6, result!D6, result!B7, result!C7, result!D7, result!B8, result!C8, result!D8, result!B9, result!C9, result!D9, result!B10, result!C10, result!D10, result!B11, result!C11, result!D11, result!B12, result!C12, result!D12\n\n\n## Skill\n### Skill: date arithmetic\n- Parse dates with datetime (try common formats); keep them as datetime objects, never strings, until the final write.\n- Day differences are (a - b).days on dates; respect inclusive/exclusive wording in the instruction. Output dates as YYYY-MM-DD (or YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS if times are involved).\n\n### Skill: writing cells\n- Write computed VALUES (not formulas) unless the task explicitly requires formula text.\n- Write every requested answer cell; an unwritten cell scores zero. Convert Python types to plain scalars (no numpy types, no datetime objects — use ISO strings).\n\n\nReply with a single Python script in a ```python fence. No prose. INIT_XLSX and OUT_XLSX are predefined. Save OUT_XLSX and print one SUMMARY_JSON line.", "completion": "{\"cells\": [{\"cell\": \"B2\", \"value\": \"N/A\", \"sheet\": \"result\"}, {\"cell\": \"C2\", \"value\": \"N/A\", \"sheet\": \"result\"}, {\"cell\": \"D2\", \"value\": \"N/A\", \"sheet\": \"result\"}, {\"cell\": \"B3\", \"value\": \"Branch Manager\", \"sheet\": \"result\"}, {\"cell\": \"C3\", \"value\": \"7768825777\", \"sheet\": \"result\"}, {\"cell\": \"D3\", \"value\": \"vidhyan@gmail.com\", \"sheet\": \"result\"}, {\"cell\": \"B4\", \"value\": \"Branch Credit Manager\", \"sheet\": \"result\"}, {\"cell\": \"C4\", \"value\": \"9592887766\", \"sheet\": \"result\"}, {\"cell\": \"D4\", \"value\": \"priyapatil.k@gmail.com\", \"sheet\": \"result\"}, {\"cell\": \"B5\", \"value\": \"N/A\", \"sheet\": \"result\"}, {\"cell\": \"C5\", \"value\": \"N/A\", \"sheet\": \"result\"}, {\"cell\": \"D5\", \"value\": \"N/A\", \"sheet\": \"result\"}, {\"cell\": \"B6\", \"value\": \"N/A\", \"sheet\": \"result\"}, {\"cell\": \"C6\", \"value\": \"N/A\", \"sheet\": \"result\"}, {\"cell\": \"D6\", \"value\": \"N/A\", \"sheet\": \"result\"}, {\"cell\": \"B7\", \"value\": \"Branch Manager\", \"sheet\": \"result\"}, {\"cell\": \"C7\", \"value\": 9999143233, \"sheet\": \"result\"}, {\"cell\": \"D7\", \"value\": \"vivekgovekar1@gmail.com\", \"sheet\": \"result\"}, {\"cell\": \"B8\", \"value\": \"Branch Manager\", \"sheet\": \"result\"}, {\"cell\": \"C8\", \"value\": \"9425493385\", \"sheet\": \"result\"}, {\"cell\": \"D8\", \"value\": \"nagarajup@yahoo.com\", \"sheet\": \"result\"}, {\"cell\": \"B9\", \"value\": \"N/A\", \"sheet\": \"result\"}, {\"cell\": \"C9\", \"value\": \"N/A\", \"sheet\": \"result\"}, {\"cell\": \"D9\", \"value\": \"N/A\", \"sheet\": \"result\"}, {\"cell\": \"B10\", \"value\": \"Branch Credit Manager\", \"sheet\": \"result\"}, {\"cell\": \"C10\", \"value\": \"9845267900\", \"sheet\": \"result\"}, {\"cell\": \"D10\", \"value\": \"krishnap@gmail.com\", \"sheet\": \"result\"}, {\"cell\": \"B11\", \"value\": \"N/A\", \"sheet\": \"result\"}, {\"cell\": \"C11\", \"value\": \"N/A\", \"sheet\": \"result\"}, {\"cell\": \"D11\", \"value\": \"N/A\", \"sheet\": \"result\"}, {\"cell\": \"B12\", \"value\": \"Branch Credit Manager\", \"sheet\": \"result\"}, {\"cell\": \"C12\", \"value\": \"7522944799\", \"sheet\": \"result\"}, {\"cell\": \"D12\", \"value\": \"harigu.p@gmail.com\", \"sheet\": \"result\"}]}", "sample_idx": 5, "latency_s": 8.9, "in_tokens": 1411, "out_tokens": 454}
{"id": "192-22", "kind": "sheet-level", "path": "codegen-readback", "system": "You write self-contained Python that edits a workbook with openpyxl ONLY. No torch, no network, no pip install, no os/sys/subprocess/pathlib. INIT_XLSX and OUT_XLSX are already defined as path strings. Load INIT_XLSX, compute the answer from the real workbook (not the preview), write the graded answer cells, save to OUT_XLSX. Print exactly one line: SUMMARY_JSON={\"status\": \"ok|error\", \"notes\": \"...\"}. Never fabricate numbers — compute them from the workbook. Allowed imports: openpyxl, datetime, math, json, re, statistics, collections, itertools, copy, decimal.", "prompt": "## Instruction\nI need a VBA code on Sheet1 that scans every populated cell in column D and checks whether the text contains any of the following keywords (case-insensitive, partial match allowed): ‘Core Activation’, ‘Core Design’, ‘Mobile Terminology’, ‘Mobile Design’, ‘Mobile Integration’, ‘Testing Layer’, ‘Testing Offshore’, ‘Carrier’, and ‘Barrier’. If a match is found, output the text “Billing PO” in the corresponding row of column F; otherwise, leave column F blank. Entries in column D may include numeric or text prefixes/suffixes (for example “123-Core Design”), which must still count as valid matches. The process should handle all rows dynamically without a fixed range, preserve existing data and formatting in all other columns. If you have to, you can solve it without VBA.\n\n## Workbook (preview — read INIT_XLSX for full data)\n### Sheet: Sheet1 (showing 71x9 of 71x9)\n\tA\tB\tC\tD\tE\tF\tG\tH\tI\n1\tSource\tCo Code\tAccount\tMAPPED\tCORE VALUE\tEXPECTED RESULT\t\t\t\n2\tTotal External\tNone\tNone\tVoIP technologies\t VoIP, IMS, MPLS, ISDN, PSTN\t\t\t\t\n3\tManufacturing\tCEXTCE\tTotal External\tCore Activation Signaling and Protocols\t SIP, ISDN, Codecs, H.323\tBilling PO\t\t\tSHORT KEYS\n4\tFront Porch Digital WWOPS\tEXT023\tManufacturing\tCore Design Wireless technologies\t GPRS, CDMA, GSM, UMTS\tBilling PO\t\t\tCore Activation\n5\t11H - Front Porch Digital WWOPS\tLB011H\tFront Porch Digital WWOPS\tMobile Terminology Network Management\t SNMP\tBilling PO\t\t\tCore Design\n6\tOutgoing Manufacturing\tEXT023\tManufacturing\tMobile Design Layer 2 Protocols\t ARP, STP, L2TP, PPP\tBilling PO\t\t\tMobile Terminology\n7\t15B - Outgoing Manufacturing\tLB015B\tOutgoing Manufacturing\tTesing  Layer 3 protocols/routing\t ICMP, BGP, ISIS, MPLS\tBilling PO\t\t\tMobile Design\n8\tWWOPS-ACME Packet\tEXT023\tManufacturing\tTesting Offshore  Infrastructure/Security\t ATM, TCP/IP, LAN/VLAN, SSH\tBilling PO\t\t\tMobile Intergration\n9\t1AF - WWOPS-ACME Packet\tLB01AF\tWWOPS-ACME Packet\tAcceptance test artifacts\t VoIP, IMS, MPLS, ISDN, PSTN\t\t\t\tTesting Layer\n10\tWWOPS -Tekelec\tEXT023\tManufacturing\tIntegration test artifacts\t SIP, ISDN, Codecs, H.323\t\t\t\tTesting Offshore\n11\t2BF - WWOPS -Tekelec \tLB02BF\tWWOPS -Tekelec\tQuality and performance artifacts\t GPRS, CDMA, GSM, UMTS\t\t\t\tCarrier\n12\tWWOPS Micros\tEXT023\tManufacturing\tFunctional test artifacts\t SNMP\t\t\t\tBarrier\n13\t3GF - WWOPS Micros\tLB03GF\tWWOPS Micros\tAlpha/Beta test artifacts\t ARP, STP, L2TP, PPP\t\t\t\t\n14\tManufacturing reclass ext. 023\tEXT023\tManufacturing\tUnit test artifacts\t ICMP, BGP, ISIS, MPLS\t\t\t\t\n15\t41B - Manufacturing reclass ext. 023\tLB041B\tManufacturing reclass ext. 023\tIntegration test artifacts\t ATM, TCP/IP, LAN/VLAN, SSH\t\t\t\t\n16\tWWOPS Tooling NPI\tEXT023\tManufacturing\tQuality and performance artifacts\t VoIP, IMS, MPLS, ISDN, PSTN\t\t\t\t\n17\t5XB - WWOPS Tooling NPI\tLB05XB\tWWOPS Tooling NPI\tRegression, load testing, sanity, etc.\t SIP, ISDN, Codecs, H.323\t\t\t\t\n18\tWWOPS Tooling Sustaining\tEXT023\tManufacturing\tInterconnection Testing\t GPRS, CDMA, GSM, UMTS\t\t\t\t\n19\t5YB - WWOPS Tooling Sustaining\tLB05YB\tWWOPS Tooling Sustaining\tConformance Testing\t SNMP\t\t\t\t\n20\tWWOPS Tooling CIP\tEXT023\tManufacturing\tCarrier IVR Testing\t ARP, ST