1\"}, {\"cell\": \"F49\", \"value\": null, \"sheet\": \"Sheet1\"}, {\"cell\": \"F50\", \"value\": null, \"sheet\": \"Sheet1\"}, {\"cell\": \"F51\", \"value\": \"Billing PO\", \"sheet\": \"Sheet1\"}, {\"cell\": \"F52\", \"value\": \"Billing PO\", \"sheet\": \"Sheet1\"}, {\"cell\": \"F53\", \"value\": \"Billing PO\", \"sheet\": \"Sheet1\"}, {\"cell\": \"F54\", \"value\": \"Billing PO\", \"sheet\": \"Sheet1\"}, {\"cell\": \"F55\", \"value\": null, \"sheet\": \"Sheet1\"}, {\"cell\": \"F56\", \"value\": \"Billing PO\", \"sheet\": \"Sheet1\"}, {\"cell\": \"F57\", \"value\": null, \"sheet\": \"Sheet1\"}, {\"cell\": \"F58\", \"value\": null, \"sheet\": \"Sheet1\"}, {\"cell\": \"F59\", \"value\": null, \"sheet\": \"Sheet1\"}, {\"cell\": \"F60\", \"value\": null, \"sheet\": \"Sheet1\"}, {\"cell\": \"F61\", \"value\": null, \"sheet\": \"Sheet1\"}, {\"cell\": \"F62\", \"value\": null, \"sheet\": \"Sheet1\"}, {\"cell\": \"F63\", \"value\": \"Billing PO\", \"sheet\": \"Sheet1\"}, {\"cell\": \"F64\", \"value\": null, \"sheet\": \"Sheet1\"}, {\"cell\": \"F65\", \"value\": null, \"sheet\": \"Sheet1\"}, {\"cell\": \"F66\", \"value\": null, \"sheet\": \"Sheet1\"}, {\"cell\": \"F67\", \"value\": null, \"sheet\": \"Sheet1\"}, {\"cell\": \"F68\", \"value\": null, \"sheet\": \"Sheet1\"}, {\"cell\": \"F69\", \"value\": null, \"sheet\": \"Sheet1\"}, {\"cell\": \"F70\", \"value\": null, \"sheet\": \"Sheet1\"}, {\"cell\": \"F71\", \"value\": null, \"sheet\": \"Sheet1\"}]}", "sample_idx": 1, "latency_s": 6.8, "in_tokens": 4388, "out_tokens": 304}
{"id": "209-30", "kind": "sheet-level", "path": "codegen-readback", "system": "You write self-contained Python that edits a workbook with openpyxl ONLY. No torch, no network, no pip install, no os/sys/subprocess/pathlib. INIT_XLSX and OUT_XLSX are already defined as path strings. Load INIT_XLSX, compute the answer from the real workbook (not the preview), write the graded answer cells, save to OUT_XLSX. Print exactly one line: SUMMARY_JSON={\"status\": \"ok|error\", \"notes\": \"...\"}. Never fabricate numbers — compute them from the workbook. Allowed imports: openpyxl, datetime, math, json, re, statistics, collections, itertools, copy, decimal.", "prompt": "## Instruction\nI have an Excel VBA issue where I'm trying to remove the last three characters from each postcode in a column, and the number of rows can range from 1 to 500,000. My current code is erroneously changing every value in the column to FALSE instead of removing the characters. Here's the code I'm using: Sub RemoveChar()\n\nDim ws As Worksheet\nDim c As Range\nSet ws = Worksheets(\"Data to Import\")\n\nFor Each c In ws.Range(\"C2\", ws.Range(\"c\" & ws.Rows.Count).End(xlUp))\nc.Value = (\"C2\") = Left(ws.Range(\"C2\"), Len(ws.Range(\"C2\")) - 3)\n\nNext c\n\nEnd Sub Can anyone explain what I'm doing wrong with this code?\n\n## Workbook (preview — read INIT_XLSX for full data)\n### Sheet: Home (showing 1x1 of 1x1)\n\tA\n1\t\n\n### Sheet: Location Matrix (showing 1x1 of 1x1)\n\tA\n1\tDate\n\n### Sheet: Data to Import (showing 120x6 of 93197x6)\n\tA\tB\tC\tD\tE\tF\n1\tDate\tURN\tLocation\t\t\t\n2\t\t\tDY8 3NQ\t\t\t\n3\t\t\tDY8 3NQ\t\t\t\n4\t\t\tDY8 3NQ\t\t\t\n5\t\t\tDY8 3NQ\t\t\t\n6\t\t\tDY8 3NQ\t\t\t\n7\t\t\tDY8 3NQ\t\t\t\n8\t\t\tDY8 3NQ\t\t\t\n9\t\t\tDY8 3NQ\t\t\t\n10\t\t\tDY8 3NQ\t\t\t\n11\t\t\tDY8 3NQ\t\t\t\n12\t\t\tDY8 3NQ\t\t\t\n13\t\t\tDY8 3NQ\t\t\t\n14\t\t\tDY8 3NQ\t\t\t\n15\t\t\tDY8 3NQ\t\t\t\n16\t\t\tDY8 3NQ\t\t\t\n17\t\t\tDY8 3NQ\t\t\t\n18\t\t\tDY8 3NQ\t\t\t\n19\t\t\tDY8 3NQ\t\t\t\n20\t\t\tDY8