}, {\"cell\": \"A84\", \"value\": \"20f\", \"sheet\": \"Sheet1\"}, {\"cell\": \"B84\", \"value\": \"06/09/2018 13:21:40\", \"sheet\": \"Sheet1\"}, {\"cell\": \"A85\", \"value\": \"20g\", \"sheet\": \"Sheet1\"}, {\"cell\": \"B85\", \"value\": \"06/09/2018 13:22:01\", \"sheet\": \"Sheet1\"}, {\"cell\": \"A86\", \"value\": \"20h\", \"sheet\": \"Sheet1\"}, {\"cell\": \"B86\", \"value\": \"06/09/2018 13:25:43\", \"sheet\": \"Sheet1\"}, {\"cell\": \"A87\", \"value\": \"20i\", \"sheet\": \"Sheet1\"}, {\"cell\": \"B87\", \"value\": \"06/09/2018 13:26:45\", \"sheet\": \"Sheet1\"}, {\"cell\": \"A88\", \"value\": \"20j\", \"sheet\": \"Sheet1\"}, {\"cell\": \"B88\", \"value\": \"06/09/2018 13:28:34\", \"sheet\": \"Sheet1\"}, {\"cell\": \"A89\", \"value\": 21, \"sheet\": \"Sheet1\"}, {\"cell\": \"B89\", \"value\": \"06/09/2018 13:38:36\", \"sheet\": \"Sheet1\"}, {\"cell\": \"A90\", \"value\": null, \"sheet\": \"Sheet1\"}, {\"cell\": \"B90\", \"value\": null, \"sheet\": \"Sheet1\"}]}", "sample_idx": 4, "latency_s": 14.9, "in_tokens": 6510, "out_tokens": 821}
{"id": "359-21", "kind": "sheet-level", "path": "codegen-readback", "system": "You write self-contained Python that edits a workbook with openpyxl ONLY. No torch, no network, no pip install, no os/sys/subprocess/pathlib. INIT_XLSX and OUT_XLSX are already defined as path strings. Load INIT_XLSX, compute the answer from the real workbook (not the preview), write the graded answer cells, save to OUT_XLSX. Print exactly one line: SUMMARY_JSON={\"status\": \"ok|error\", \"notes\": \"...\"}. Never fabricate numbers — compute them from the workbook. Allowed imports: openpyxl, datetime, math, json, re, statistics, collections, itertools, copy, decimal.", "prompt": "## Instruction\nI created a macro to delete rows in which specific conditions are met in a particular column. The macro operates properly with small datasets but becomes very slow with larger ones. Is there a way to improve or modify the macro to speed up the process? Here is the code for the macro I'm using: Sub Delete_rows() Application.ScreenUpdating = False Application.DisplayAlerts = False Dim sh1 As Worksheet Dim lastrow As Long Dim i As Long Set sh1 = ThisWorkbook.Worksheets(\"Delete\") lastrow = sh1.Cells(Rows.Count, \"A\").End(xlUp).Row For i = lastrow To 2 Step -1 If sh1.Cells(i, \"B\").Value = \"STATIONERY\" Or sh1.Cells(i, \"B\").Value = \"VEGETABLES\" Then sh1.Cells(i, \"A\").EntireRow.Delete End If Next i Application.ScreenUpdating = True Application.DisplayAlerts = True End Sub\n\n## Workbook (preview — read INIT_XLSX for full data)\n### Sheet: Delete (showing 9x2 of 9x2)\n\tA\tB\n1\tCUSTOMER NAME\tTYPE\n2\tB&CO\tGROCERY\n3\tC& CO\tGROCERY\n4\tD& CO\tSTATIONERY\n5\tE& CO\tGROCERY\n6\tF& CO\tGROCERY\n7\tG& CO\tVEGETABLES\n8\tH& CO\tHARDWARE\n9\tI & CO\tELECTRICALS\n\n### Answer range (pinned, 18 cells)\nDelete!A1=CUSTOMER NAME\nDelete!B1=TYPE\nDelete!A2=B&CO\nDelete!B2=GROCERY\nDelete!A3=C& CO\nDelete!B3=GROCERY\nDelete!A4=D& CO\nDelete!B4=STATIONERY\nDelete!A5=E& CO\nDelete!B5=GROCERY\nDelete!A6=F& CO\nDelete!B6=GROCERY\nDelete!A7=G& CO\nDelete!B7=VEGETABLES\nDelete!A8=H& CO\nDelete!B8=HARDWARE\nDelete!A9=I & CO\nDelete!B9=ELECTRICALS\n\n## Answer range\nSheet: Delete\nCells: 'Delete'!A1:B9\nData range: A1:B9\nGraded cells: Delete!A1, Delete!B1, Delete!A2, Delete!B2, Delete!A3, Delete!B3, Delete!A4, Delete!B4, Delete!A5, Delete!B5, Delete!A6, Delete!B6, Delete!A7, Delete!B7, Delete!A8, Delete!B8, Delete!A9, Delete!B9\n\n\n## Skill\n### Skill: sheet reorganization\n- Never run/emit VBA or macros; implement the equivalent Python transform on the sheets.\n- When deleting rows, iterate bottom-up so indices stay valid; preserve the header row and any rows above it unless told otherwise.\n- Keep sheet names byte-exact (quotes/spaces matter). Do not create helper sheets or write outside the requested target range.\n\n### Skill: writing cells\n- Write computed VALUES (not formulas) unless the task explicitly requires formula text.\n- Write every requested answer cell; an unwritten cell scores zero. Convert Python types to plain scalars (no numpy types, no datetime objects — use ISO strings).\n\n\nReply with a single Python script in a ```python fence. No prose. INIT_XLSX and OUT_XLSX are predefined. Save OUT_XLSX and print one SUMMARY_JSON line.", "completion": "{\"cells\": [{\"cell\": \"A1\", \"value\": \"CUSTOMER NAME\", \"sheet\": \"Delete\"}, {\"cell\": \"B1\", \"value\": \"TYPE\", \"sheet\": \"Delete\"}, {\"cell\": \"A2\", \"value\": \"B&CO\", \"sheet\": \"Delete\"}, {\"cell\": \"B2\", \"value\": \"GROCERY\", \"sheet\": \"Delete\"}, {\"cell\": \"A3\", \"value\": \"C& CO\", \"sheet\": \"Delete\"}, {\"cell\": \"B3\", \"value\": \"GROCERY\", \"sheet\": \"Delete\"}, {\"cell\": \"A4\", \"value\": \"E& CO\", \"sheet\": \"Delete\"}, {\"cell\": \"B4\", \"value\": \"GROCERY\", \"sheet\": \"Delete\"}, {\"cell\": \"A5\", \"value\": \"F& CO\", \"sheet\": \"Delete\"}, {\"cell\": \"B5\", \"value\": \"GROCERY\", \"sheet\": \"Delete\"}, {\"cell\": \"A6\", \"value\": \"H& CO\", \"sheet\": \"Delete\"}, {\"cell\": \"B6\", \"value\": \"HARDWARE\", \"sheet\": \"Delete\"}, {\"cell\": \"A7\", \"value\": \"I & CO\", \"sheet\": \"Delete\"}, {\"cell\": \"B7\", \"value\": \"ELECTRICALS\", \"sheet\": \"Delete\"}, {\"cell\": \"A8\", \"value\": null, \"sheet\": \"Delete\"}, {\"cell\": \"B8\", \"value\": null, \"sheet\": \"Delete\"}, {\"cell\": \"A9\", \"value\": null, \"sheet\": \"Delete\"}, {\"cell\": \"B9\", \"value\": null, \"sheet\": \"Delete\"}]}", "sample_idx": 2, "latency_s": 7.5, "in_tokens": 930, "out_tokens": 339}
{"id": "367-23", "kind": "sheet-level", "path": "codegen-readback", "system": "You write self-contained Python that edits a workbook with openpyxl ONLY. No torch, no network, no pip install, no os/sys/subprocess/pathlib. INIT_XLSX and OUT_XLSX are already defined as path strings. Load INIT_XLSX, compute the answer from the real workbook (not the preview), write the graded answer cells, save to OUT_XLSX. Print exactly one line: SUMMARY_JSON={\"status\": \"ok|error\", \"notes\": \"...\"}. Never fabricate numbers — compute them from the workbook. Allowed imports: openpyxl, datetime, math, json, re, statistics, collections, itertools, copy, decimal.", "prompt": "## Instruction\nI have written a macro that should delete rows from a worksheet named 'Final Recon Items' where the values in column D (4th column), containing positive or negative values of 0.01, sum up to zero. The macro I've attempted to use is not working as expected; it fails to delete the relevant rows even though the sum of the values appears to be zero. However, a forum expert pointed out that the actual values include slight variations due to precision, such as -1.00000000093132E-02, -9.99999999476131E-03, 9.9999999802094E-03, and 1.00000000020373E-02, which are not strictly equal to zero. The expert suggested using an absolute value check with a threshold of 0.011 to identify values that are effectively zero for the purpose of deletion, but implementing this results in a runtime error 'Type Mismatch' and I am unable to resolve it. Additionally, it was mentioned that in the first row of column 4 there's a non-numeric value 'Amount' which could be related to the issue. I need help in correcting the macro code to perform the intended row-deletion operation accurately.\n\n## Workbook (preview — read INIT_XLSX for full data)\n### Sheet: final Recon Items (showing 5x4 of 5x4)\n\tA\tB\tC\tD\n1\tDate\tBranch\tRef\tAmount\n2\t2021-03-09 00:00:00\tBr1\t\t0.0100000000020373\n3\t17/09/2021\tBr1\t\t0.0099999999802094\n4\t20/09/2021\tBr1\t\t-0.00999999999476131\n5\t23/09/2021\tBr1\t\t-0.0100000000093132\n\n### Answer range (pinned, 20 cells)\nfinal Recon Items!A1=Date\nfinal Recon Items!B1=Branch\nfinal Recon Items!C1=Ref\nfinal Recon Items!D1=Amount\nfinal Recon Items!A2=2021-03-09 00:00:00\nfinal Recon Items!B2=Br1\nfinal Recon Items!C2=\nfinal Recon Items!D2=0.0100000000020373\nfinal Recon Items!A3=17/09/2021\nfinal Recon Items!B3=Br1\nfinal Recon Items!C3=\nfinal Recon Items!D3=0.0099999999802094\nfinal Recon Items!A4=20/09/2021\nfinal Recon Items!B4=Br1\nfinal Recon Items!C4=\nfinal Recon Items!D4=-0.00999999999476131\nfinal Recon Items!A5=23/09/2021\nfinal Recon Items!B5=Br1\nfinal Recon Items!C5=\nfinal Recon Items!D5=-0.0100000000093132\n\n## Answer range\nSheet: final Recon Items\nCells: 'final Recon Items'!A1:D5\nData range: A1:D5\nGraded cells: final Recon Items!A1, final Recon Items!B1, final Recon Items!C1, final Recon Items!D1, final Recon Items!A2, final Recon Items!B2, final Recon Items!C2, final Recon Items!D2, final Recon Items!A3, final Recon Items!B3, final Recon Items!C3, final Recon Items!D3, final Recon Items!A4, final Recon Items!B4, final Recon Items!C4, final Recon Items!D4, final Recon Items!A5, final Recon Items!B5, final Recon Items!C5, final Recon Items!D5\n\n\n## Skill\n### Skill: sheet reorganization\n- Never run/emit VBA or macros; implement the equivalent Python transform on the sheets.\n- When deleting rows, iterate bottom-up so indices stay valid; preserve the header row and any rows above it unless told otherwise.\n- Keep sheet names byte-exact (quotes/spaces matter). Do not create helper sheets or write outside the requested target range.\n\n### Skill: writing cells\n- Write computed VALUES (not formulas) unless the task explicitly requires formula text.\n- Write every requested answer cell; an unwritten cell scores zero. Convert Python types to plain scalars (no numpy types, no datetime objects — use ISO strings).\n\n\nReply with a single Python script in a ```python fence. No prose. INIT_XLSX and OUT_XLSX are predefined. Save OUT_XLSX and print one SUMMARY_JSON line.", "completion": "{\"cells\": [{\"cell\": \"A1\", \"value\": \"Date\", \"sheet\": \"final Recon Items\"}, {\"cell\": \"B1\", \"value\": \"Branch\", \"sheet\": \"final Recon Items\"}, {\"cell\": \"C1\", \"value\": \"Ref\", \"sheet\": \"final Recon Items\"}, {\"cell\": \"D1\", \"value\": \"Amount\", \"sheet\": \"final Recon Items\"}, {\"cell\": \"A2\", \"value\": null, \"sheet\": \"final Recon Items\"}, {\"cell\": \"B2\", \"value\": null, \"sheet\": \"final Recon Items\"}, {\"cell\": \"C2\", \"value\": null, \"sheet\": \"final Recon Items\"}, {\"cell\": \"D2\", \"value\": null, \"sheet\": \"final Recon Items\"}, {\"cell\": \"A3\", \"value\": null, \"sheet\": \"final Recon Items\"}, {\"cell\": \"B3\", \"value\": null, \"sheet\": \"final Recon Items\"}, {\"cell\": \"C3\", \"value\": null, \"sheet\": \"final Recon Items\"}, {\"cell\": \"D3\", \"value\": null, \"sheet\": \"final Recon Items\"}, {\"cell\": \"A4\", \"value\": null, \"sheet\": \"final Recon Items\"}, {\"cell\": \"B4\", \"value\": null, \"sheet\": \"final Recon Items\"}, {\"cell\": \"C4\", \"value\": null, \"sheet\": \"final Recon Items\"}, {\"cell\": \"D4\", \"value\": null, \"sheet\": \"final Recon Items\"}, {\"cell\": \"A5\", \"value\": null, \"sheet\": \"final Recon Items\"}, {\"cell\": \"B5\", \"value\": null, \"sheet\": \"final Recon Items\"}, {\"cell\": \"C5\", \"value\": null, \"sheet\": \"final Recon Items\"}, {\"cell\": \"D5\", \"value\": null, \"sheet\": \"final Recon Items\"}]}", "sample_idx": 5, "latency_s": 11.2, "in_tokens": 1322, "out_tokens": 557}
{"id": "367-23", "kind": "sheet-level", "path": "codegen-readback", "system": "You write self-contained Python that edits a workbook with openpyxl ONLY. No torch, no network, no pip install, no os/sys/subprocess/pathlib. INIT_XLSX and OUT_XLSX are already defined as path strings. Load INIT_XLSX, compute the answer from the real workbook (not the preview), write the graded answer cells, save to OUT_XLSX. Print exactly one line: SUMMARY_JSON={\"status\": \"ok|error\", \"notes\": \"...\"}. Never fabricate numbers — compute them from the workbook. Allowed imports: openpyxl, datetime, math, json, re, statistics, collections, itertools, copy, decimal.", "prompt": "## Instruction\nI have written a macro that should delete rows from a worksheet named 'Final Recon Items' where the values in column D (4th column), containing positive or negative values of 0.01, sum up to zero. The macro I've attempted to use is not working as expected; it fails to delete the relevant rows even though the sum of the values appears to be zero. However, a forum expert pointed out that the actual values include slight variations due to precision, such as -1.00000000093132E-02, -9.99999999476131E-03, 9.9999999802094E-03, and 1.00000000020373E-02, which are not strictly equal to zero. The expert suggested using an absolute value check with a threshold of 0.011 to identify values that are effectively zero for the purpose of deletion, but implementing this results in a runtime error 'Type Mismatch' and I am unable to resolve it. Additionally, it was mentioned that in the first row of column 4 there's a non-numeric value 'Amount' which could be related to the issue. I need help in correcting the macro code to perform the intended row-deletion operation accurately.\n\n## Workbook (preview — read INIT_XLSX for full data)\n### Sheet: final Recon Items (showing 5x4 of 5x4)\n\tA\tB\tC\tD\n1\tDate\tBranch\tRef\tAmount\n2\t2021-03-09 00:00:00\tBr1\t\t0.0100000000020373\n3\t17/09/2021\tBr1\t\t0.0099999999802094\n4\t20/09/2021\tBr1\t\t-0.00999999999476131\n5\t23/09/2021\tBr1\t\t-0.0100000000093132\n\n### Answer range (pinned, 20 cells)\nfinal Recon Items!A1=Date\nfinal Recon Items!B1=Branch\nfinal Recon Items!C1=Ref\nfinal Recon Items!D1=Amount\nfinal Recon Items!A2=2021-03-09 00:00:00\nfinal Recon Items!B2=Br1\nfinal Recon Items!C2=\nfinal Recon Items!D2=0.0100000000020373\nfinal Recon Items!A3=17/09/2021\nfinal Recon Items!B3=Br1\nfinal Recon Items!C3=\nfinal Recon Items!D3=0.0099999999802094\nfinal Recon Items!A4=20/09/2021\nfinal Recon Items!B4=Br1\nfinal Recon Items!C4=\nfinal Recon Items!D4=-0.00999999999476131\nfinal Recon Items!A5=23/09/2021\nfinal Recon Items!B5=Br1\nfinal Recon Items!C5=\nfinal Recon Items!D5=-0.0100000000093132\n\n## Answer range\nSheet: final Recon Items\nCells: 'final Recon Items'!A1:D5\nData range: A1:D5\nGraded cells: final Recon Items!A1, final Recon Items!B1, final Recon Items!C1, final Recon Items!D1, final Recon Items!A2, final Recon Items!B2, final Recon Items!C2, final Recon Items!D2, final Recon Items!A3, final Recon Items!B3, final Recon Items!C3, final Recon Items!D3, final Recon Items!A4, final Recon Items!B4, final Recon Items!C4, final Recon Items!D4, final Recon Items!A5, final Recon Items!B5, final Recon Items!C5, final Recon Items!D5\n\n\n## Skill\n### Skill: sheet reorganization\n- Never run/emit VBA or macros; implement the equivalent Python transform on the sheets.\n- When deleting rows, iterate bottom-up so indices stay valid; preserve the header row and any rows above it unless told otherwise.\n- Keep sheet names byte-exact (quotes/spaces matter). Do not create helper sheets or write outside the requested target range.\n\n### Skill: writing cells\n- Write computed VALUES (not formulas) unless the task explicitly requires formula text.\n- Write every requested answer cell; an unwritten cell scores zero. Convert Python types to plain scalars (no numpy types, no datetime objects — use ISO strings).\n\n\nReply with a single Python script in a ```python fence. No prose. INIT_XLSX and OUT_XLSX are predefined. Save OUT_XLSX and print one SUMMARY_JSON line.", "completion": "{\"cells\": [{\"cell\": \"A1\", \"value\": \"Date\", \"sheet\": \"final Recon Items\"}, {\"cell\": \"B1\", \"value\": \"Branch\", \"sheet\": \"final Recon Items\"}, {\"cell\": \"C1\", \"value\": \"Ref\", \"sheet\": \"final Recon Items\"}, {\"cell\": \"D1\", \"value\": \"Amount\", \"sheet\": \"final Recon Items\"}, {\"cell\": \"A2\", \"value\": \"2021-03-09T00:00:00\", \"sheet\": \"final Recon Items\"}, {\"cell\": \"B2\", \"value\": \"Br1\", \"sheet\": \"final Recon Items\"}, {\"cell\": \"C2\", \"value\": null, \"sheet\": \"final Recon Items\"}, {\"cell\": \"D2\", \"value\": 0.0100000000020373, \"sheet\": \"final Recon Items\"}, {\"cell\": \"A3\", \"value\": \"17/09/2021\", \"sheet\": \"final Recon Items\"}, {\"cell\": \"B3\", \"value\": \"Br1\", \"sheet\": \"final Recon Items\"}, {\"cell\": \"C3\", \"value\": null, \"sheet\": \"final Recon Items\"}, {\"cell\": \"D3\", \"value\": 0.0099999999802094, \"sheet\": \"final Recon Items\"}, {\"cell\": \"A4\", \"value\": \"20/09/2021\", \"sheet\": \"final Recon Items\"}, {\"cell\": \"B4\", \"value\": \"Br1\", \"sheet\": \"final Recon Items\"}, {\"cell\": \"C4\", \"value\": null, \"sheet\": \"final Recon Items\"}, {\"cell\": \"D4\", \"value\": -0.00999999999476131, \"sheet\": \"final Recon Items\"}, {\"cell\": \"A5\", \"value\": \"23/09/2021\", \"sheet\": \"final Recon Items\"}, {\"cell\": \"B5\", \"value\": \"Br1\", \"sheet\": \"final Recon Items\"}, {\"cell\": \"C5\", \"value\": null, \"sheet\": \"final Recon Items\"}, {\"cell\": \"D5\", \"value\": -0.0100000000093132, \"sheet\": \"final Recon Items\"}]}", "sample_idx": 1, "latency_s": 21.2, "in_tokens": 1322, "out_tokens": 1256}
