{"id": "398-14", "kind": "sheet-level", "path": "codegen-readback", "system": "You write self-contained Python that edits a workbook with openpyxl ONLY. No torch, no network, no pip install, no os/sys/subprocess/pathlib. INIT_XLSX and OUT_XLSX are already defined as path strings. Load INIT_XLSX, compute the answer from the real workbook (not the preview), write the graded answer cells, save to OUT_XLSX. Print exactly one line: SUMMARY_JSON={\"status\": \"ok|error\", \"notes\": \"...\"}. Never fabricate numbers — compute them from the workbook. Allowed imports: openpyxl, datetime, math, json, re, statistics, collections, itertools, copy, decimal.", "prompt": "## Instruction\nI have data across multiple sheets where I need to match and sum values from columns that are repeated across these sheets. To do this, I need to insert a column called 'BALANCE' which subtracts the 'RET' value from the 'SALE' columns. Whenever I add new sheets that have the same structure, the macro should be able to adapt to include them. The results, along with headers, should be compiled in the 'collection' sheet. Reference the values and logic of the existing rows, then complete the table for any missing information from the other sheets by adding it to the bottom of the current table, but do not alter the order of the original rows.  Make sure that rows are aggregated across all sheets where “TY” and “OR” are the same.  Additionally, instead of showing a formula in column G, it should display the calculated value, and any empty cells should show a hyphen instead of a zero, and any negatives should have a text color hex code of #FF0000, and column headers should be un-bolded and left-side aligned.  All other formatting should remain unchanged, and any new data added should match. Columns A, E, F, and G now align right, while columns B, C, and D align left. Make all text unbold, and font Calibri 11pts.\n\n## Workbook (preview — read INIT_XLSX for full data)\n### Sheet: STA (showing 7x6 of 7x6)\n\tA\tB\tC\tD\tE\tF\n1\tITEM\tBR\tTY\tOR\tSALE\tRET\n2\t1.0\tFR\tBANANA\tTT\t200.0\t10.0\n3\t2.0\tFR\tAPPLE\tLL\t100.0\t20.0\n4\t3.0\tFR\tPEAR\tNN\t10.0\t-\n5\t4.0\tFR\tBANANA\tQQ\t20.0\t-\n6\t5.0\tVEG\tTOMATO\tSS\t12.0\t-\n7\t6.0\tVEG\tTOMATO\tAA\t12.0\t12.0\n\n### Sheet: RPA (showing 7x6 of 7x6)\n\tA\tB\tC\tD\tE\tF\n1\tITEM\tBR\tTY\tOR\tSALE\tRET\n2\t1.0\tFR\tBANANA\tTT\t100.0\t5.0\n3\t2.0\tFR\tAPPLE\tLL\t50.0\t5.0\n4\t3.0\tFR\tPEAR\tNN\t20.0\t-\n5\t4.0\tFR\tBANANA\tQQ\t10.0\t-\n6\t5.0\tVEG\tTOMATO\tSS\t10.0\t5.0\n7\t6.0\tVEG\tTOMATO\tAA\t5.0\t\n\n### Sheet: SR (showing 7x5 of 7x5)\n\tA\tB\tC\tD\tE\n1\tITEM\tBR\tTY\tOR\tSALE\n2\t1.0\tFR\tAPPLE\tLL\t120.0\n3\t2.0\tFR\tPEAR\tNN\t30.0\n4\t3.0\tFR\tBANANA\tQQ\t40.0\n5\t4.0\tVEG\tTOMATO\tSS\t50.0\n6\t5.0\tVEG\tTOMATO\tAA\t5.0\n7\t6.0\tVEG\tONION\tAA1\t6.0\n\n### Sheet: SS (showing 8x5 of 8x5)\n\tA\tB\tC\tD\tE\n1\tITEM\tBR\tTY\tOR\tRET\n2\t1.0\tFR\tBANANA\tTT\t5.0\n3\t2.0\tFR\tAPPLE\tLL\t2.0\n4\t3.0\tFR\tPEAR\tNN\t3.0\n5\t4.0\tFR\tBANANA\tQQ\t-\n6\t5.0\tVEG\tTOMATO\tSS\t5.0\n7\t6.0\tVEG\tONION\tAA1\t-\n8\t7.0\tVEG\tPOTATO\tAA2\t5.0\n\n### Sheet: COLLECTION (showing 8x7 of 8x7)\n\tA\tB\tC\tD\tE\tF\tG\n1\tITEM\tBR\tTY\tOR\tSALE\tRET\tBALANCE\n2\t1.0\tFR\tBANANA\tTT\t300.0\t20.0\t280\n3\t2.0\tFR\tAPPLE\tLL\t270.0\t27.0\t243\n4\t3.0\tFR\tPEAR\tNN\t60.0\t3.0\t57\n5\t4.0\tFR\tBANANA\tQQ\t70.0\t0.0\t70\n6\t5.0\tVEG\tTOMATO\tSS\t72.0\t10.0\t62\n7\t6.0\tVEG\tTOMATO\tAA\t22.0\t12.0\t10\n8\t7.0\tVEG\tONION\tAA1\t6.0\t0.0\t6\n\n### Answer range (pinned, 56 cells)\nCOLLECTION!A2=1.0\nCOLLECTION!B2=FR\nCOLLECTION!C2=BANANA\nCOLLECTION!D2=TT\nCOLLECTION!E2=300.0\nCOLLECTION!F2=20.0\nCOLLECTION!G2=280\nCOLLECTION!A3=2.0\nCOLLECTION!B3=FR\nCOLLECTION!C3=APPLE\nCOLLECTION!D3=LL\nCOLLECTION!E3=270.0\nCOLLECTION!F3=27.0\nCOLLECTION!G3=243\nCOLLECTION!A4=3.0\nCOLLECTION!B4=FR\nCOLLECTION!C4=PEAR\nCOLLECTION!D4=NN\nCOLLECTION!E4=60.0\nCOLLECTION!F4=3.0\nCOLLECTION!G4=57\nCOLLECTION!A5=4.0\nCOLLECTION!B5=FR\nCOLLECTION!C5=BANANA\nCOLLECTION!D5=QQ\nCOLLECTION!E5=70.0\nCOLLECTION!F5=0.0\nCOLLECTION!G5=70\nCOLLECTION!A6=5.0\nCOLLECTION!B6=VEG\nCOLLECTION!C6=TOMATO\nCOLLECTION!D6=SS\nCOLLECTION!E6=72.0\nCOLLECTION!F6=10.0\nCOLLECTION!G6=62\nCOLLECTION!A7=6.0\nCOLLECTION!B7=VEG\nCOLLECTION!C7=TOMATO\nCOLLECTION!D7=AA\nCOLLECTION!E7=22.0\nCOLLECTION!F7=12.0\nCOLLECTION!G7=10\nCOLLECTION!A8=7.0\nCOLLECTION!B8=VEG\nCOLLECTION!C8=ONION\nCOLLECTION!D8=AA1\nCOLLECTION!E8=6.0\nCOLLECTION!F8=0.0\nCOLLECTION!G8=6\nCOLLECTION!A9=\nCOLLECTION!B9=\nCOLLECTION!C9=\nCOLLECTION!D9=\nCOLLECTION!E9=\nCOLLECTION!F9=\nCOLLECTION!G9=\n\n## Answer range\nSheet: COLLECTION\nCells: 'COLLECTION'!A2:G9\nData range: A1:G9\nGraded cells: COLLECTION!A2, COLLECTION!B2, COLLECTION!C2, COLLECTION!D2, COLLECTION!E2, COLLECTION!F2, COLLECTION!G2, COLLECTION!A3, COLLECTION!B3, COLLECTION!C3, COLLECTION!D3, COLLECTION!E3, COLLECTION!F3, COLLECTION!G3, COLLECTION!A4, COLLECTION!B4, COLLECTION!C4, COLLECTION!D4, COLLECTION!E4, COLLECTION!F4, COLLECTION!G4, COLLECTION!A5, COLLECTION!B5, COLLECTION!C5, COLLECTION!D5, COLLECTION!E5, COLLECTION!F5, COLLECTION!G5, COLLECTION!A6, COLLECTION!B6, COLLECTION!C6, COLLECTION!D6, COLLECTION!E6, COLLECTION!F6, COLLECTION!G6, COLLECTION!A7, COLLECTION!B7, COLLECTION!C7, COLLECTION!D7, COLLECTION!E7, COLLECTION!F7, COLLECTION!G7, COLLECTION!A8, COLLECTION!B8, COLLECTION!C8, COLLECTION!D8, COLLECTION!E8, COLLECTION!F8, COLLECTION!G8, COLLECTION!A9, COLLECTION!B9, COLLECTION!C9, COLLECTION!D9, COLLECTION!E9, COLLECTION!F9, COLLECTION!G9\n\n\n## Skill\n### Skill: aggregation / pivot\n- Group rows with a dict keyed by the condition columns, then aggregate with sum/count/min/max as instructed. Every condition must hold (AND), including date or time windows.\n- When comparing times of day, compare hour/minute only if the date component is irrelevant. Write one output value per expected output cell, in order.\n\n### Skill: sheet reorganization\n- Never run/emit VBA or macros; implement the equivalent Python transform on the sheets.\n- When deleting rows, iterate bottom-up so indices stay valid; preserve the header row and any rows above it unless told otherwise.\n- Keep sheet names byte-exact (quotes/spaces matter). Do not create helper sheets or write outside the requested target range.\n\n\nReply with a single Python script in a ```python fence. No prose. INIT_XLSX and OUT_XLSX are predefined. Save OUT_XLSX and print one SUMMARY_JSON line.", "completion": "{\"cells\": [{\"cell\": \"A2\", \"value\": 1, \"sheet\": \"COLLECTION\"}, {\"cell\": \"B2\", \"value\": \"FR\", \"sheet\": \"COLLECTION\"}, {\"cell\": \"C2\", \"value\": \"BANANA\", \"sheet\": \"COLLECTION\"}, {\"cell\": \"D2\", \"value\": \"TT\", \"sheet\": \"COLLECTION\"}, {\"cell\": \"E2\", \"value\": 300, \"sheet\": \"COLLECTION\"}, {\"cell\": \"F2\", \"value\": 20, \"sheet\": \"COLLECTION\"}, {\"cell\": \"G2\", \"value\": 280, \"sheet\": \"COLLECTION\"}, {\"cell\": \"A3\", \"value\": 2, \"sheet\": \"COLLECTION\"}, {\"cell\": \"B3\", \"value\": \"FR\", \"sheet\": \"COLLECTION\"}, {\"cell\": \"C3\", \"value\": \"APPLE\", \"sheet\": \"COLLECTION\"}, {\"cell\": \"D3\", \"value\": \"LL\", \"sheet\": \"COLLECTION\"}, {\"cell\": \"E3\", \"value\": 270, \"sheet\": \"COLLECTION\"}, {\"cell\": \"F3\", \"value\": 27, \"sheet\": \"COLLECTION\"}, {\"cell\": \"G3\", \"value\": 243, \"sheet\": \"COLLECTION\"}, {\"cell\": \"A4\", \"value\": 3, \"sheet\": \"COLLECTION\"}, {\"cell\": \"B4\", \"value\": \"FR\", \"sheet\": \"COLLECTION\"}, {\"cell\": \"C4\", \"value\": \"PEAR\", \"sheet\": \"COLLECTION\"}, {\"cell\": \"D4\", \"value\": \"NN\", \"sheet\": \"COLLECTION\"}, {\"cell\": \"E4\", \"value\": 60, \"sheet\": \"COLLECTION\"}, {\"cell\": \"F4\", \"value\": 3, \"sheet\": \"COLLECTION\"}, {\"cell\": \"G4\", \"value\": 57, \"sheet\": \"COLLECTION\"}, {\"cell\": \"A5\", \"value\": 4, \"sheet\": \"COLLECTION\"}, {\"cell\": \"B5\", \"value\": \"FR\", \"sheet\": \"COLLECTION\"}, {\"cell\": \"C5\", \"value\": \"BANANA\", \"sheet\": \"COLL