{"id": "399-14", "kind": "sheet-level", "path": "codegen-readback", "system": "You write self-contained Python that edits a workbook with openpyxl ONLY. No torch, no network, no pip install, no os/sys/subprocess/pathlib. INIT_XLSX and OUT_XLSX are already defined as path strings. Load INIT_XLSX, compute the answer from the real workbook (not the preview), write the graded answer cells, save to OUT_XLSX. Print exactly one line: SUMMARY_JSON={\"status\": \"ok|error\", \"notes\": \"...\"}. Never fabricate numbers — compute them from the workbook. Allowed imports: openpyxl, datetime, math, json, re, statistics, collections, itertools, copy, decimal.", "prompt": "## Instruction\nUse '等线' font throughout the entire sheet. I need a VB (Visual Basic) Code to split recorded employee hours into regular hours and overtime hours. The hours worked by employees are listed in Column N of an Excel worksheet. If the value in any cell of Column N is less than or equal to 40, it should remain unchanged. However, if the value exceeds 40, then the cell in Column N should display 40, and the amount over 40 should be hardcoded to the corresponding cell in Column O. For example, if cell N12 shows 52.62, then after the code runs, N12 should display 40 and O12 should show the difference, which would be 12.62. If you don't have access to VB, use the tools you currently have. Use #,##0.## number formatting in columns N, O, and P except for whole numbers. Use General formatting for whole numbers.\n\n## Workbook (preview — read INIT_XLSX for full data)\n### Sheet: Sheet1 (showing 23x16 of 23x16)\n\tA\tB\tC\tD\tE\tF\tG\tH\tI\tJ\tK\tL\tM\tN\tO\tP\n1\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n2\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n3\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n4\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n5\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n6\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tStoreName\tName\tREG\tOT\tTips\n7\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tStore\tAriel Greenway\t39.499999046325684\t\t71.78999999999999\n8\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tStore\tAtalie Luangxay\t32.47000050544739\t\t64.61\n9\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tStore\tCamille Arnold\t24.28000020980835\t\t11.959999999999999\n10\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tStore\tChloee Heidbrider\t33.15000081062317\t\t17.27\n11\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tStore\tDreamia Sao\t16.46999979019165\t\t11.620000000000001\n12\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tStore\tElias Aristile\t52.6199996471405\t\t44.339999999999996\n13\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tStore\tElizabeth Vega\t38.27000069618225\t\t36.46000000000001\n14\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tStore\tEmily Edwards\t27.41000008583069\t\t50.37\n15\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tStore\tGeshanti Smith\t41.419999837875366\t\t51.38\n16\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tStore\tJessie Elliot\t41.03999978303909\t\t17.25\n17\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tStore\tJyra Walker\t30.889999866485596\t\t42.93000000000001\n18\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tStore\tKierra Collins\t56.139999866485596\t\t70.65\n19\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tStore\tMacey Recor\t14.509999752044678\t\t22.8\n20\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tStore\tMcKenzie Gower\t11.980000019073486\t\t9.89\n21\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tStore\tNia Sanders\t42.0600004196167\t\t84.92000000000002\n22\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tStore\tRachel Leet\t56.85000026226044\t\t21.360000000000003\n23\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tStore\tShelby Freshwater\t36.19000017642975\t\t15.49\n\n### Answer range (pinned, 34 cells)\nSheet1!N7=39.499999046325684\nSheet1!O7=\nSheet1!N8=32.47000050544739\nSheet1!O8=\nSheet1!N9=24.28000020980835\nSheet1!O9=\nSheet1!N10=33.15000081062317\nSheet1!O10=\nSheet1!N11=16.46999979019165\nSheet1!O11=\nSheet1!N12=52.6199996471405\nSheet1!O12=\nSheet1!N13=38.27000069618225\nSheet1!O13=\nSheet1!N14=27.41000008583069\nSheet1!O14=\nSheet1!N15=41.419999837875366\nSheet1!O15=\nSheet1!N16=41.03999978303909\nSheet1!O16=\nSheet1!N17=30.889999866485596\nSheet1!O17=\nSheet1!N18=56.139999866485596\nSheet1!O18=\nSheet1!N19=14.509999752044678\nSheet1!O19=\nSheet1!N20=11.980000019073486\nSheet1!O20=\nSheet1!N21=42.0600004196167\nSheet1!O21=\nSheet1!N22=56.85000026226044\nSheet1!O22=\nS